{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-004", "category": "reasoning", "title": "New York to London across the DST gap", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2431, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 133, "reasoning_tokens": 46, "input_tokens": 105, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 249, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "14:30, 13:30, 13:30, 13:30, 14:30", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "14:30, 13:30, 13:30, 13:30, 14:30"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjb7c7972b-d029-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjb686e8f1-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:08:25-0500", "answer": "New York switches to daylight saving time on March 8, 2026; London switches on March 29. London is therefore 5 hours ahead on March 2 and March 30, but only 4 hours ahead for the three intervening meetings.\n\nANSWER: 14:30, 13:30, 13:30, 13:30, 14:30"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-001", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Six-digit numbers with digit sum 27", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4456, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 283, "reasoning_tokens": 92, "input_tokens": 45, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 610, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "55252", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "55252"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjb6c89da0-d029-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjb686e8f0-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:08:25-0500", "answer": "Represent each integer as a six-digit string, allowing leading zeros. We need to count solutions to\n\\[\nd_1+\\cdots+d_6=27,\\qquad 0\\le d_i\\le9.\n\\]\nThe all-zero string does not qualify, so this counts exactly the integers in the given range.\n\nWithout the upper bounds, stars and bars gives \\(\\binom{32}{5}\\) solutions. By inclusion\u2013exclusion, subtract solutions with a digit at least 10 and add back those with two such digits. Three such digits are impossible since their sum would exceed 27.\n\nThus the count is\n\\[\n\\binom{32}{5}-6\\binom{22}{5}+\\binom62\\binom{12}{5}\n=201376-158004+11880\n=55252.\n\\]\n\nANSWER: 55252"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-005", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Divisible by exactly two of 4, 6 and 9", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4978, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 332, "reasoning_tokens": 85, "input_tokens": 56, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 625, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "83334", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "83334"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjb6b64e0f-d029-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjb6871002-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:08:25-0500", "answer": "The pairwise least common multiples are\n\\[\n\\operatorname{lcm}(4,6)=12,\\quad\n\\operatorname{lcm}(4,9)=36,\\quad\n\\operatorname{lcm}(6,9)=18.\n\\]\nThe least common multiple of all three is \\(36\\).\n\nAdding the counts for the three pairs counts each integer divisible by exactly two once, but each integer divisible by all three three times. Thus the desired count is\n\\[\n\\left\\lfloor\\frac{1{,}000{,}000}{12}\\right\\rfloor\n+\\left\\lfloor\\frac{1{,}000{,}000}{36}\\right\\rfloor\n+\\left\\lfloor\\frac{1{,}000{,}000}{18}\\right\\rfloor\n-3\\left\\lfloor\\frac{1{,}000{,}000}{36}\\right\\rfloor\n=83{,}333+55{,}555-2(27{,}777)\n=83{,}334.\n\\]\n\nANSWER: 83334"}
