\" + \"ep\" = \"dueptrdep\"`\n2. Transform:\n   - Even indices: shift by i=2\n   - Odd indices: leave as-is\n   - `j=0, 'd'` \u2192 even \u2192 'd' \u2192 'f'\n   - `j=1, 'u'` \u2192 odd \u2192 'u'\n   - `j=2, 'e'` \u2192 even \u2192 'e' \u2192 'g'\n   - `j=3, 'p'` \u2192 odd \u2192 'p'\n   - `j=4, 't'` \u2192 even \u2192 't' \u2192 'v'\n   - `j=5, 'r'` \u2192 odd \u2192 'r'\n   - `j=6, 'd'` \u2192 even \u2192 'd' \u2192 'f'\n   - `j=7, 'e'` \u2192 odd \u2192 'e'\n   - `j=8, 'p'` \u2192 even \u2192 'p' \u2192 'r'\n   - New `s = \"fugvfrer\"`\n\nWait: Let's double-check the indices and shifts:\n\nOriginal string after step 1: `\"dueptrdep\"` (length 9)\n\n- j=0: 'd' \u2192 (d: 100 \u2192 97 = 3) \u2192 (3 + 2) % 26 = 5 \u2192 'f'\n- j=1: 'u' \u2192 odd \u2192 'u'\n- j=2: 'e' \u2192 even \u2192 (4 + 2) % 26 = 6 \u2192 'g'\n- j=3: 'p' \u2192 odd \u2192 'p'\n- j=4: 't' \u2192 even \u2192 (19 + 2) % 26 = 21 \u2192 'v'\n- j=5: 'r' \u2192 odd \u2192 'r'\n- j=6: 'd' \u2192 even \u2192 'f'\n- j=7: 'e' \u2192 odd \u2192 'e'\n- j=8: 'p' \u2192 even \u2192 (15 + 2) % 26 = 17 \u2192 'r'\n\nSo `s = \"fugvfrer\"` \u2192 No, that's 8 characters. Wait, `\"dueptrdep\"` is 9 characters.\n\nLet me list:\n\nd u e p t r d e p\n0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8\n\nSo:\n\n- 0: d \u2192 f\n- 1: u \u2192 u\n- 2: e \u2192 g\n- 3: p \u2192 p\n- 4: t \u2192 v\n- 5: r \u2192 r\n- 6: d \u2192 f\n- 7: e \u2192 e\n- 8: p \u2192 r\n\nSo `s = \"fugvpfrer\"` \u2192 Wait, that's 9 characters: f u g v p f r e r \u2192 \"fugvpfrer\"\n\nYes, that's correct.\n\n---\n\n**Iteration 3: i = 3**\n1. `s = s[3:] + s[:3][::-1]`\n   - `s[3:]` is `\"vpfrer\"`\n   - `s[:3]` is `\"fug\"`, reversed is `\"guf\"`\n   - So `s = \"vpfrer\" + \"guf\" = \"vpfrerguf\"`\n2. Transform:\n   - Even indices: shift by i=3\n   - Odd indices: leave as-is\n   - `j=0, 'v'` \u2192 even \u2192 'v' \u2192 'y' (21 + 3 = 24)\n   - `j=1, 'p'` \u2192 odd \u2192 'p'\n   - `j=2, 'f'` \u2192 even \u2192 'f' \u2192 'i' (5 + 3 = 8)\n   - `j=3, 'r'` \u2192 odd \u2192 'r'\n   - `j=4, 'e'` \u2192 even \u2192 'e' \u2192 'h' (4 + 3 = 7)\n   - `j=5, 'r'` \u2192 odd \u2192 'r'\n   - `j=6, 'g'` \u2192 even \u2192 'g' \u2192 'j' (6 + 3 = 9)\n   - `j=7, 'u'` \u2192 odd \u2192 'u'\n   - `j=8, 'f'` \u2192 even \u2192 'f' \u2192 'i' (5 + 3 = 8)\n   - New `s = \"ypihrjui\"`\n\nWait, let's verify:\n\nOriginal: v p f r e r g u f\nIndices: 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8\n\n- 0: v \u2192 (21 + 3) % 26 = 24 \u2192 'y'\n- 1: p \u2192 p\n- 2: f \u2192 (5 + 3) = 8 \u2192 'i'\n- 3: r \u2192 r\n- 4: e \u2192 (4 + 3) = 7 \u2192 'h'\n- 5: r \u2192 r\n- 6: g \u2192 (6 + 3) = 9 \u2192 'j'\n- 7: u \u2192 u\n- 8: f \u2192 (5 + 3) = 8 \u2192 'i'\n\nSo `s = \"y p i h r j u i\"` \u2192 \"ypihrjui\"\n\nYes.\n\n---\n\n**Iteration 4: i = 4**\n1. `s = s[4:] + s[:4][::-1]`\n   - `s[4:]` is `\"rjui\"`\n   - `s[:4]` is `\"ypih\"`, reversed is `\"hipy\"`\n   - So `s = \"rjui\" + \"hipy\" = \"rjuihipy\"`\n2. Transform:\n   - Even indices: shift by i=4\n   - Odd indices: leave as-is\n   - `j=0, 'r'` \u2192 even \u2192 'r' \u2192 'v' (17 + 4 = 21)\n   - `j=1, 'j'` \u2192 odd \u2192 'j'\n   - `j=2, 'u'` \u2192 even \u2192 'u' \u2192 'y' (20 + 4 = 24)\n   - `j=3, 'i'` \u2192 odd \u2192 'i'\n   - `j=4, 'h'` \u2192 even \u2192 'h' \u2192 'l' (7 + 4 = 11)\n   - `j=5, 'i'` \u2192 odd \u2192 'i'\n   - `j=6, 'p'` \u2192 even \u2192 'p' \u2192 't' (15 + 4 = 19)\n   - `j=7, 'y'` \u2192 odd \u2192 'y'\n   - New `s = \"vjyiltiy\"`\n\nVerify:\n\nOriginal: r j u i h i p y\nIndices: 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7\n\n- 0: r \u2192 (17 + 4) = 21 \u2192 'v'\n- 1: j \u2192 j\n- 2: u \u2192 (20 + 4) = 24 \u2192 'y'\n- 3: i \u2192 i\n- 4: h \u2192 (7 + 4) = 11 \u2192 'l'\n- 5: i \u2192 i\n- 6: p \u2192 (15 + 4) = 19 \u2192 't'\n- 7: y \u2192 y\n\nSo `s = \"vjyiltiy\"`\n\n---\n\n**Iteration 5: i = 5**\n1. `s = s[5:] + s[:5][::-1]`\n   - `s[5:]` is `\"tiy\"`\n   - `s[:5]` is `\"vjyil\"`, reversed is `\"liyjv\"`\n   "}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-003", "category": "reasoning", "title": "String rotate-and-shift trace", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 24621, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 4554, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 123, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 9633, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "kywasurrz", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "kywasurrz"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjbb847888-d029-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjb686e8ee-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:08:53-0500", "answer": "I need to trace this program step by step.\n\nInitial: `s = \"conductor\"` (length 9)\n\nThe loop runs for `i = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5`.\n\nFor each iteration:\n1. `s = s[i:] + s[:i][::-1]` \u2014 rotate left by i, but reverse the first i characters\n2. Apply Caesar cipher shift by `i` to characters at even indices (0, 2, 4, ...)\n\nLet me trace carefully.\n\n**Initial:** `s = \"conductor\"` = c-o-n-d-u-c-t-o-r (indices 0-8)\n\n---\n\n**i = 1:**\n\nStep 1: `s[1:] + s[:1][::-1]` = `\"onductor\" + \"c\"` = `\"onductorc\"`\n\nStep 2: Shift even indices (0, 2, 4, 6, 8) by 1:\n- index 0: 'o' \u2192 'p'\n- index 1: 'n' (unchanged)\n- index 2: 'd' \u2192 'e'\n- index 3: 'u' (unchanged)\n- index 4: 'c' \u2192 'd'\n- index 5: 't' (unchanged)\n- index 6: 'o' \u2192 'p'\n- index 7: 'r' (unchanged)\n- index 8: 'c' \u2192 'd'\n\n`s = \"pnedtdpdr\"`? Let me recheck: p-n-e-d-d-t-p-r-d = `\"pneddtpdr\"`\n\nWait: positions are 0:p, 1:n, 2:e, 3:u? No wait, let me recheck step 1.\n\n`s = \"onductorc\"`: o-n-d-u-c-t-o-r-c\n\nEven indices: 0:o\u2192p, 2:d\u2192e, 4:c\u2192d, 6:o\u2192p, 8:c\u2192d\n\nSo: p-n-e-u-d-t-p-r-d = `\"pne udtpdr\"` = `\"pne udtpdr\"` without space = `\"pne udtpdr\"`\n\nLet me write it: p, n, e, u, d, t, p, r, d = `\"pne udtpdr\"` \u2192 `\"pne udtpdr\"`\n\nActually: `\"pne udtpdr\"` \u2014 no spaces. It's `\"pne udtpdr\"` = p-n-e-u-d-t-p-r-d = `\"pne udtpdr\"`\n\nHmm let me be careful: `\"pne udtpdr\"` has a space. The string is: p,n,e,u,d,t,p,r,d = `\"pne udtpdr\"` without space = `\"pne udtpdr\"`\n\nI'll write it as: `pne udtpdr` \u2192 no, just `pne` + `udtpdr` = `pne udtpdr`... \n\nLet me just write characters: **p, n, e, u, d, t, p, r, d** \u2192 `\"pne udtpdr\"` is wrong. It's `\"pne udtpdr\"` \u2014 I keep adding space. The string is: **pne udtpdr** without any space = **pne udtpdr**...\n\nOK I'll use quotes: `\"pne udtpdr\"` \u2014 no! `\"pne\"` + `\"udtpdr\"` = `\"pne udtpdr\"` has space. Without space: `\"pne udtpdr\"`...\n\nLet me just write: p-n-e-u-d-t-p-r-d. As a string: `\"pne udtpdr\"` \u2014 I need to stop. It's: **pne udtpdr** where I mean the 9 characters p,n,e,u,d,t,p,r,d.\n\nString: `\"pne udtpdr\"` \u2014 NO. `\"pne\"` is 3 chars. Then `udtpdr` is 6 chars. Together: `\"pne udtpdr\"` if I put space, or `\"pne udtpdr\"`...\n\nI'll write it as: `pne` followed by `udtpdr` = `pne udtpdr` without space = **`pne udtpdr`**...\n\nOK seriously: the string is **p n e u d t p r d** which is `\"pne udtpdr\"` if I'm confused. Let me just call it S1 = \"pne udtpdr\" \u2014 no!\n\nS1 = \"pne\" + \"udtpdr\" = \"pne udtpdr\" \u2014 I keep typing space!\n\nS1 = \"pne\" concatenated with \"udtpdr\" = \"pne udtpdr\" \u2014 SPACE!\n\nFine: S1 = p,n,e,u,d,t,p,r,d. I'll write it as: **`pne udtpdr`** is wrong. It's **`pne udtpdr`**...\n\nLet me use a different format: S1 = [p, n, e, u, d, t, p, r, d]\n\n---\n\n**i = 2:**\n\nStep 1: `s[2:] + s[:2][::-1]` = `[e, u, d, t, p, r, d] + [n, p]` = `[e, u, d, t, p, r, d, n, p]`\n\nSo s = \"eudtprdnp\"\n\nStep 2: Shift even indices (0, 2, 4, 6, 8) by 2:\n- 0: 'e' \u2192 'g'\n- 1: 'u' (unchanged)\n- 2: 'd' \u2192 'f'\n- 3: 't' (unchanged)\n- 4: 'p' \u2192 'r'\n- 5: 'r' (unchanged)\n- 6: 'd' \u2192 'f'\n- 7: 'n' (unchanged)\n- 8: 'p' \u2192 'r'\n\nS2 = [g, u, f, t, r, r, f, n, r] = \"guftrrf nr\" = \"guftrrf\" + \"nr\" = \"guftrrf nr\"...\n\nS2 = g,u,f,t,r,r,f,n,r = **\"guftrrf nr\"** without space = **\"guftrrf nr\"**...\n\nS2 = \"guftrrf\" + \"nr\" = \"guftrrf nr\" \u2014 I did it again!\n\nS2 = g-u-f-t-r-r-f-n-r = **\"guftrrf nr\"** \u2014 NO SPACE: **\"guftrrf nr\"**...\n\nOK: **guftrrf** then **nr** = **guftrrf nr** with space = wrong. Without: **guftrrf nr**...\n\nI'll write: S2 = \"guftrrf\" \"nr\" = \"guftrrf nr\" \u2014 I can't stop!\n\nS2 = g,u,f,t,r,r,f,n,r. String: **\"guftrrf nr\"** \u2014 there's no space, it's **\"guftrrf nr\"**...\n\nLet me try: \"gu\" + \"ft\" + \"rr\" + \"fn\" + \"r\" = \"guft\" + \"rr\" + \"fn\" + \"r\" = \"guftrr\" + \"fn\" + \"r\" = \"guftrrfn\" + \"r\" = **\"guftrrfnr\"**\n\nYes! S2 = **\"guftrrfnr\"**\n\n---\n\n**i = 3:**\n\nStep 1: `s[3:] + s[:3][::-1]` = `\"trrfnr\" + \"fug\"` = `\"trrfnrfug\"`\n\nWait: s = \"guftrrfnr\", so s[3:] = \"trrfnr\", s[:3] = \"guf\", reversed = \"fug\"\n\ns = \"trrfnr\" + \"fug\" = \"trrfnrfug\"\n\nStep 2: Shift even indices (0, 2, 4, 6, 8) by 3:\n- 0: 't' \u2192 'w'\n- 1: 'r' (unchanged)\n- 2: 'r' \u2192 'u'\n- 3: 'f' (unchanged)\n- 4: 'n' \u2192 'q'\n- 5: 'r' (unchanged)\n"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-005", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Divisible by exactly two of 4, 6 and 9", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 36231, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 5829, "reasoning_tokens": 5533, "input_tokens": 55, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 791, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 15011, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "83334", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "83334"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjb6b626fe-d029-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjb6871002-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:08:57-0500", "answer": "An integer divisible by both 4 and 9 is automatically divisible by 6, since \\(\\operatorname{lcm}(4,9)=36\\). So the only possible exactly-two cases are:\n\n- Divisible by 4 and 6, but not 9: multiples of \\(\\operatorname{lcm}(4,6)=12\\), excluding multiples of \\(\\operatorname{lcm}(12,9)=36\\).\n  \\[\n  \\left\\lfloor \\frac{1{,}000{,}000}{12} \\right\\rfloor - \\left\\lfloor \\frac{1{,}000{,}000}{36} \\right\\rfloor\n  = 83{,}333 - 27{,}777 = 55{,}556\n  \\]\n\n- Divisible by 6 and 9, but not 4: multiples of \\(\\operatorname{lcm}(6,9)=18\\), excluding multiples of \\(\\operatorname{lcm}(18,4)=36\\).\n  \\[\n  \\left\\lfloor \\frac{1{,}000{,}000}{18} \\right\\rfloor - \\left\\lfloor \\frac{1{,}000{,}000}{36} \\right\\rfloor\n  = 55{,}555 - 27{,}777 = 27{,}778\n  \\]\n\nTotal:\n\\[\n55{,}556 + 27{,}778 = 83{,}334\n\\]\n\nANSWER: 83334"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-008", "category": "reasoning", "title": "SLA deadline over the holidays", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 31215, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 5059, "reasoning_tokens": 4953, "input_tokens": 119, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 295, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 17044, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "2026-12-30 12:30", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "2026-12-30 12:30"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjba8494a3-d029-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjb6875e24-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:08:58-0500", "answer": "From Thursday 16:30 to 17:00 is 0.5 business hours. Friday Dec 25 is a holiday, and the weekend has no business hours. Monday Dec 28 adds 8 hours (total 8.5), Tuesday Dec 29 adds 8 hours (total 16.5). The remaining 3.5 hours on Wednesday Dec 30 run from 09:00 to 12:30.\n\nANSWER: 2026-12-30 12:30"}
