{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-003", "category": "reasoning", "title": "String rotate-and-shift trace", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 68343, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 9297, "reasoning_tokens": 9139, "input_tokens": 123, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 413, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 22549, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "kywasurrz", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "kywasurrz"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjbb849f99-d029-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjb686e8ee-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:37-0500", "answer": "Tracing by hand:\n\n- Start: `s = \"conductor\"`\n- After each iteration, the string is rearranged, then even-indexed characters are shifted forward by `i`.\n\nIteration results:\n\n1. `i=1`: `\"pneudsman\"`? Actually exact letters: `p n e u d t p r d`\n2. `i=2`: `g u f t r r f n r`\n3. `i=3`: `w r u f q r i u j`\n4. `i=4`: `u r m u n f y r a`\n5. `i=5`: `k y w a s u r r z`\n\nSo the final printed string is:\n\nANSWER: kywasurrz"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-009", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Round-robin scheduler with arrivals", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4225, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 347, "reasoning_tokens": 112, "input_tokens": 248, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 501, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "b:9,d:11,a:16,c:18,e:20", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "b:9,d:11,a:16,c:18,e:20"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje5600b59-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje5344b9d-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:43-0500", "answer": "Arrivals are admitted **before** the running job is requeued, so newly arrived jobs go ahead of it.\n\n| Run interval | Job | Remaining afterward | Completion |\n|---|---|---:|---|\n| 0\u20132 | a | 3 | |\n| 2\u20134 | b | 1 | |\n| 4\u20136 | c | 4 | |\n| 6\u20138 | a | 1 | |\n| 8\u20139 | b | 0 | `b:9` |\n| 9\u201311 | d | 0 | `d:11` |\n| 11\u201313 | c | 2 | |\n| 13\u201315 | e | 2 | |\n| 15\u201316 | a | 0 | `a:16` |\n| 16\u201318 | c | 0 | `c:18` |\n| 18\u201320 | e | 0 | `e:20` |\n\nThe completion strings are joined with commas.\n\nANSWER: b:9,d:11,a:16,c:18,e:20"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-015", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Drawing all three marble colors", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2628, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 182, "reasoning_tokens": 50, "input_tokens": 79, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 352, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "4/7", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "4/7"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje62d6db8-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje53499c2-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:43-0500", "answer": "There are \\(\\binom{9}{4}=126\\) equally likely ways to draw four marbles.\n\nFor all three colors to appear, one color must appear twice and the other two once. The number of favorable draws is\n\\[\n\\binom42\\binom31\\binom21\n+\\binom41\\binom32\\binom21\n+\\binom41\\binom31\\binom22\n=36+24+12=72.\n\\]\nThus the probability is \\(\\frac{72}{126}=\\frac47\\).\n\nANSWER: 4/7"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-015", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Drawing all three marble colors", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3249, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 214, "reasoning_tokens": 88, "input_tokens": 79, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 326, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "4/7", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "4/7"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje62d6dbb-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje53499c2-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:43-0500", "answer": "There are \\(\\binom{9}{4}=126\\) equally likely sets of four marbles.\n\nFor all three colors to appear, one color must occur twice and the other two once. The number of favorable sets is\n\\[\n\\binom{4}{2}(3)(2)+(4)\\binom{3}{2}(2)+(4)(3)\\binom{2}{2}\n=36+24+12=72.\n\\]\n\nThus the probability is \\(\\frac{72}{126}=\\frac47\\).\n\nANSWER: 4/7"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-015", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Drawing all three marble colors", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2867, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 467, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 79, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1152, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "4/7", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "4/7"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje62d6db9-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje53499c2-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:43-0500", "answer": "I need to find the probability that all three colors appear when drawing 4 marbles from a bag containing 4 red, 3 blue, and 2 green marbles.\n\n## Setting Up the Problem\n\nTotal marbles: 4 + 3 + 2 = 9\nTotal ways to draw 4 marbles: $\\binom{9}{4} = \\frac{9!}{4!5!} = \\frac{9 \\cdot 8 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 6}{24} = 126$\n\n## Finding Favorable Outcomes\n\nFor all three colors to appear in 4 marbles, the color distribution must be (2,1,1) in some order \u2014 one color appears twice, and the other two colors appear once each.\n\n**Case 1: 2 red, 1 blue, 1 green**\n$$\\binom{4}{2}\\binom{3}{1}\\binom{2}{1} = 6 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 2 = 36$$\n\n**Case 2: 1 red, 2 blue, 1 green**\n$$\\binom{4}{1}\\binom{3}{2}\\binom{2}{1} = 4 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 2 = 24$$\n\n**Case 3: 1 red, 1 blue, 2 green**\n$$\\binom{4}{1}\\binom{3}{1}\\binom{2}{2} = 4 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 1 = 12$$\n\nTotal favorable outcomes: $36 + 24 + 12 = 72$\n\n## Calculating the Probability\n\n$$P = \\frac{72}{126} = \\frac{72 \\div 18}{126 \\div 18} = \\frac{4}{7}$$\n\nLet me verify: $72 = 8 \\cdot 9 = 2^3 \\cdot 3^2$ and $126 = 2 \\cdot 63 = 2 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 7 = 2 \\cdot 3^2 \\cdot 7$\n\nGCD is $2 \\cdot 3^2 = 18$. So $\\frac{72}{126} = \\frac{4}{7}$ \u2713\n\nANSWER: 4/7"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-013", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Most jobs finished by their deadlines", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4769, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 358, "reasoning_tokens": 162, "input_tokens": 185, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 530, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "6", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "6"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje58c8311-d029-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje53499c4-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:44-0500", "answer": "The maximum is **6 jobs**.\n\nOne schedule achieving this is:\n\n| Job | Completion time | Deadline | On time? |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| J2 | 2 | 5 | Yes |\n| J4 | 5 | 9 | Yes |\n| J6 | 7 | 11 | Yes |\n| J8 | 10 | 13 | Yes |\n| J5 | 16 | 18 | Yes |\n| J7 | 20 | 20 | Yes |\n| J1 | 24 | 6 | No |\n| J3 | 29 | 14 | No |\n\n**Why seven is impossible:** All eight jobs require 29 hours. Even omitting the longest job (6 hours), any seven require at least 23 hours. Since every deadline is at most 20, seven jobs cannot all finish on time.\n\nANSWER: 6"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-012", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Counting paths in a dependency graph", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3310, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 243, "reasoning_tokens": 42, "input_tokens": 135, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 417, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "26", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "26"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje640809a-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje53472ae-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:44-0500", "answer": "Let \\(p(v)\\) be the number of directed paths from vertex \\(v\\) to \\(T\\). Set \\(p(T)=1\\); for every other vertex, sum \\(p\\) over its outgoing neighbors.\n\nWorking backward:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\np(G)&=p(H)=1,\\\\\np(D)&=p(G)+p(T)=2,\\\\\np(E)&=p(G)+p(H)=2,\\\\\np(F)&=p(H)+p(T)=2,\\\\\np(B)&=p(D)+p(E)+p(F)=6,\\\\\np(A)&=p(D)+p(E)+p(B)=10,\\\\\np(C)&=p(E)+p(F)+p(B)=10.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nThus \\(p(S)=p(A)+p(B)+p(C)=10+6+10=26\\).\n\nANSWER: 26"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-016", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Four houses: owners and pets", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5346, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 367, "reasoning_tokens": 164, "input_tokens": 236, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 679, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "Leo, Jon, Ivy, Kim, fish, bird, cat, dog", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "Leo, Jon, Ivy, Kim, fish, bird, cat, dog"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje59b8dd3-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje53499c1-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:44-0500", "answer": "Jon must live in house 2 or 3, since the fish is immediately to his left and the blue house immediately to his right.\n\nIf Jon lived in house 3, Ivy and Kim would occupy houses 1 and 2, leaving Leo in house 4\u2014with no room for the red house to Leo\u2019s right. Thus Jon lives in house 2.\n\nIvy and Kim then occupy houses 3 and 4, and Leo occupies house 1. The blue house is 3, so the green house must be 2 or 4. Only green in house 2 allows Kim to live at least two houses away, placing Kim in house 4 and Ivy in house 3.\n\nThe fish is in house 1, the dog in house 4, and the bird in house 2 next to Ivy. The cat is therefore in house 3.\n\nANSWER: Leo, Jon, Ivy, Kim, fish, bird, cat, dog"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-012", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Counting paths in a dependency graph", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4483, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 652, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 134, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1392, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "26", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "26"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje640809b-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje53472ae-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:44-0500", "answer": "I need to find all directed paths from S to T in this DAG.\n\nLet me first list all edges:\n- S\u2192A, S\u2192B, S\u2192C\n- A\u2192D, A\u2192E, A\u2192B\n- B\u2192D, B\u2192E, B\u2192F\n- C\u2192E, C\u2192F, C\u2192B\n- D\u2192G, D\u2192T\n- E\u2192G, E\u2192H\n- F\u2192H, F\u2192T\n- G\u2192T\n- H\u2192T\n\nLet me use dynamic programming. I'll compute the number of paths from each node to T.\n\n**Base cases (nodes with direct edge to T):**\n- D\u2192T: 1 path (direct)\n- F\u2192T: 1 path (direct)\n- G\u2192T: 1 path (direct)\n- H\u2192T: 1 path (direct)\n\n**Working backwards:**\n\n**G:** G\u2192T, so paths(G) = 1\n\n**H:** H\u2192T, so paths(H) = 1\n\n**F:** F\u2192H, F\u2192T\n- paths(F) = paths(H) + paths(T direct) = 1 + 1 = 2\n\n**E:** E\u2192G, E\u2192H\n- paths(E) = paths(G) + paths(H) = 1 + 1 = 2\n\n**D:** D\u2192G, D\u2192T\n- paths(D) = paths(G) + 1 = 1 + 1 = 2\n\n**C:** C\u2192E, C\u2192F, C\u2192B\n- paths(C) = paths(E) + paths(F) + paths(B)\n\n**B:** B\u2192D, B\u2192E, B\u2192F\n- paths(B) = paths(D) + paths(E) + paths(F) = 2 + 2 + 2 = 6\n\n**A:** A\u2192D, A\u2192E, A\u2192B\n- paths(A) = paths(D) + paths(E) + paths(B) = 2 + 2 + 6 = 10\n\nNow back to **C:**\n- paths(C) = paths(E) + paths(F) + paths(B) = 2 + 2 + 6 = 10\n\n**S:** S\u2192A, S\u2192B, S\u2192C\n- paths(S) = paths(A) + paths(B) + paths(C) = 10 + 6 + 10 = 26\n\nLet me verify by checking a few paths manually or re-checking calculations.\n\nRe-checking B: B\u2192D (2 paths), B\u2192E (2 paths), B\u2192F (2 paths) = 6 \u2713\n\nRe-checking A: A\u2192D (2), A\u2192E (2), A\u2192B (6) = 10 \u2713\n\nRe-checking C: C\u2192E (2), C\u2192F (2), C\u2192B (6) = 10 \u2713\n\nRe-checking S: S\u2192A (10), S\u2192B (6), S\u2192C (10) = 26 \u2713\n\nANSWER: 26"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-011", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Shortest route that must pass through D", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3625, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 183, "reasoning_tokens": 64, "input_tokens": 163, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 345, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "13", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "13"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje6a9a2c0-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje53472b0-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:45-0500", "answer": "The shortest route meeting the conditions is:\n\n**A \u2192 C \u2192 D \u2192 E \u2192 F \u2192 G \u2192 H**\n\nIts total travel time is \\(1 + 5 + 1 + 2 + 1 + 3 = 13\\) minutes.\n\nThe shortest way from A to D takes 6 minutes (A \u2192 C \u2192 D), and the shortest way from D to H takes 7 minutes (D \u2192 E \u2192 F \u2192 G \u2192 H). These segments share only D, so no location is visited twice.\n\nANSWER: 13"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-012", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Counting paths in a dependency graph", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4490, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 243, "reasoning_tokens": 79, "input_tokens": 135, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 343, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "26", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "26"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje640809c-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje53472ae-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:45-0500", "answer": "Let \\(p(v)\\) be the number of directed paths from \\(v\\) to \\(T\\). Working backward, \\(p(v)\\) is the sum of the counts for its outgoing neighbors:\n\n- \\(p(T)=1\\)\n- \\(p(G)=p(H)=1\\)\n- \\(p(D)=p(E)=p(F)=2\\)\n- \\(p(B)=p(D)+p(E)+p(F)=6\\)\n- \\(p(A)=p(D)+p(E)+p(B)=10\\)\n- \\(p(C)=p(E)+p(F)+p(B)=10\\)\n\nThus,\n\\[\np(S)=p(A)+p(B)+p(C)=10+6+10=26.\n\\]\n\nANSWER: 26"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-013", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Most jobs finished by their deadlines", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6588, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 458, "reasoning_tokens": 308, "input_tokens": 185, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 395, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "6", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "6"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje58c8313-d029-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje53499c4-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:46-0500", "answer": "The maximum is **6 jobs**.\n\nOne feasible schedule is:\n\n| Job | Completion time | Deadline |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| J2 | 2 | 5 |\n| J4 | 5 | 9 |\n| J6 | 7 | 11 |\n| J8 | 10 | 13 |\n| J5 | 16 | 18 |\n| J7 | 20 | 20 |\n\nAll six finish on time. J1 and J3 can run afterward.\n\nSeven on-time jobs are impossible: all deadlines are at most 20, but even the seven shortest jobs require \\(29-6=23\\) hours.\n\nANSWER: 6"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-009", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Round-robin scheduler with arrivals", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 7997, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 517, "reasoning_tokens": 283, "input_tokens": 248, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 497, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "b:9,d:11,a:16,c:18,e:20", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "b:9,d:11,a:16,c:18,e:20"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje560326a-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje5344b9d-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:47-0500", "answer": "New arrivals are admitted **before** the current job is requeued. Tracing each run:\n\n| Time interval | Job | Remaining work | Completion |\n|---|---|---:|---|\n| 0\u20132 | a | 3 | |\n| 2\u20134 | b | 1 | |\n| 4\u20136 | c | 4 | |\n| 6\u20138 | a | 1 | |\n| 8\u20139 | b | 0 | `b:9` |\n| 9\u201311 | d | 0 | `d:11` |\n| 11\u201313 | c | 2 | |\n| 13\u201315 | e | 2 | |\n| 15\u201316 | a | 0 | `a:16` |\n| 16\u201318 | c | 0 | `c:18` |\n| 18\u201320 | e | 0 | `e:20` |\n\nThe completion strings are joined with commas, without spaces.\n\nANSWER: b:9,d:11,a:16,c:18,e:20"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-011", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Shortest route that must pass through D", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5339, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 299, "reasoning_tokens": 194, "input_tokens": 163, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 262, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "13", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "13"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje6a9a2c2-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje53472b0-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:47-0500", "answer": "The fastest route to D is **A \u2192 C \u2192 D**, taking \\(1+5=6\\) minutes.\n\nFrom D, the fastest route to H is **D \u2192 E \u2192 F \u2192 G \u2192 H**, taking \\(1+2+1+3=7\\) minutes.\n\nCombined, **A \u2192 C \u2192 D \u2192 E \u2192 F \u2192 G \u2192 H** visits no location twice and takes \\(6+7=13\\) minutes.\n\nANSWER: 13"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-011", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Shortest route that must pass through D", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6029, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 823, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 163, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1854, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "13", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "13"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje6a97baf-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje53472b0-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:48-0500", "answer": "I need to find the minimum travel time from A to H that passes through D, with no location visited twice.\n\nFirst, let me identify all paths from A to D, then from D to H, ensuring no repeated locations.\n\n**Paths from A to D:**\n- A->D: 7 minutes\n- A->C->D: 1 + 5 = 6 minutes\n- A->B->... no direct B->D\n- A->C->B->... no B->D\n\nSo paths A to D: A->D (7), A->C->D (6)\n\n**Paths from D to H (without revisiting locations):**\nFrom D, I can go to E or G.\n\nD->E->F->H: 1 + 2 + 8 = 11\nD->E->F->G->H: 1 + 2 + 1 + 3 = 7\nD->E->H: 1 + 12 = 13\nD->G->H: 6 + 3 = 9\n\nAlso check D->E->F->G->H uses E,F,G,H - all distinct from D.\n\nNow I need to combine A-to-D paths with D-to-H paths, ensuring no location is visited twice overall.\n\n**Option 1: A->D (7), then D to H**\n- A->D->E->F->G->H: locations A,D,E,F,G,H - all distinct! Time: 7 + 1 + 2 + 1 + 3 = 14\n- A->D->E->F->H: A,D,E,F,H - distinct. Time: 7 + 1 + 2 + 8 = 18\n- A->D->E->H: A,D,E,H - distinct. Time: 7 + 1 + 12 = 20\n- A->D->G->H: A,D,G,H - distinct. Time: 7 + 6 + 3 = 16\n\n**Option 2: A->C->D (6), then D to H**\nLocations used so far: A, C, D. Cannot use C again.\n\n- A->C->D->E->F->G->H: A,C,D,E,F,G,H - all distinct! Time: 6 + 1 + 2 + 1 + 3 = 13\n- A->C->D->E->F->H: A,C,D,E,F,H - distinct. Time: 6 + 1 + 2 + 8 = 17\n- A->C->D->E->H: A,C,D,E,H - distinct. Time: 6 + 1 + 12 = 19\n- A->C->D->G->H: A,C,D,G,H - distinct. Time: 6 + 6 + 3 = 15\n\n**Option 3: A->C->B->... to D?** No path from B to D.\n\nLet me check if there are other A to D paths:\n- A->B->E->... no E->D\n- A->B->G->... no G->D\n\nWhat about A->C->B->E->... no E->D, and A->C->F->... no F->D.\n\nSo only A->D and A->C->D reach D.\n\nThe minimum is **13 minutes** via A->C->D->E->F->G->H.\n\nLet me verify: A->C (1), C->D (5), D->E (1), E->F (2), F->G (1), G->H (3) = 1+5+1+2+1+3 = 13. \u2713\n\nLocations: A, C, D, E, F, G, H - all distinct, passes through D. \u2713\n\nANSWER: 13"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-016", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Four houses: owners and pets", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 8542, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1399, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 237, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 4083, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "Leo, Jon, Ivy, Kim, fish, bird, cat, dog", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "Leo, Jon, Ivy, Kim, fish, bird, cat, dog"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje59b8dd4-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje53499c1-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:48-0500", "answer": "I need to solve this step-by-step, tracking owners, colors, and pets for houses 1-4.\n\nLet me start with the constraints and work through them.\n\n**Key constraints:**\n- Ivy and Kim are next door to each other\n- Jon lives immediately to the left of the blue house (so Jon is in house n, blue is in house n+1)\n- Red house is to the right of Leo's house\n- Leo is not in green house\n- Kim lives at least two houses away from green house (so |Kim - green| \u2265 2)\n- Dog lives at least two houses away from Jon (|dog - Jon| \u2265 2)\n- Fish lives immediately to the left of Jon's house (fish in house n, Jon in house n+1)\n- Bird lives next door to Ivy\n\nFrom \"fish immediately left of Jon\" and \"Jon immediately left of blue\":\n- Fish is in house n, Jon in house n+1, blue in house n+2\n\nSo we have: Fish, Jon, Blue in consecutive houses. This means Jon can only be in house 2 or 3.\n\n**Case 1: Jon in house 2**\n- Fish in house 1, Jon in house 2, Blue in house 3\n\n**Case 2: Jon in house 3**\n- Fish in house 2, Jon in house 3, Blue in house 4\n\nLet me try **Case 1: Jon in house 2, Fish in house 1, Blue in house 3**\n\nDog is at least 2 houses from Jon (house 2), so dog is in house 4 (house 1 is only 1 away, house 3 is 1 away, house 4 is 2 away). So dog in house 4.\n\nPets so far: House 1: Fish, House 2: ?, House 3: ?, House 4: Dog\nRemaining pets: cat, bird for houses 2 and 3.\n\nBird is next door to Ivy. Ivy and Kim are next door to each other.\n\nOwners: Jon is in house 2. Remaining: Ivy, Kim, Leo for houses 1, 3, 4.\n\nIvy and Kim must be adjacent. Possible pairs: (1,3)? No, not adjacent. (3,4)? Yes. (1,?) - house 1 is only adjacent to house 2 (Jon).\n\nSo Ivy and Kim must be in houses 3 and 4 (in some order), leaving Leo in house 1.\n\nLeo in house 1. Red is to the right of Leo, so red is in house 2, 3, or 4. But house 3 is blue. So red is in house 2 or 4.\n\nLeo is not in green house. House 1 has Leo, so house 1 is not green.\n\nKim is at least 2 houses from green. Kim is in house 3 or 4.\n\nIf Kim in house 3: green must be in house 1 (distance 2) or... house 5 doesn't exist. So green in house 1. But Leo is in house 1, and Leo is not in green. Contradiction.\n\nIf Kim in house 4: green must be in house 1 or 2 (distance \u2265 2). House 1: Leo, not green (Leo not in green). So green in house 2. But house 2 is Jon, and we need to check colors.\n\nWait - let me check: if Kim in house 4, then Ivy in house 3. Green in house 2 (distance 2 from Kim). House 2 is Jon's house, color green.\n\nColors: House 2: green, House 3: blue. Remaining: red, white for houses 1 and 4.\nRed is to the right of Leo (house 1), so red in house 4, white in house 1.\n\nCheck: Leo in house 1 (white), not green \u2713\n\nNow pets: House 1: Fish, House 4: Dog. Houses 2,3 have cat and bird.\nBird is next door to Ivy. Ivy is in house 3. So bird is in house 2 or 4. House 4 has dog, so bird in house 2. Cat in house 3.\n\nCheck: Bird (house 2) is next door to Ivy (house 3) \u2713\n\nLet me verify all constraints:\n- Houses: 1=Leo, 2=Jon, 3=Ivy, 4=Kim\n- Colors: 1=white, 2=green, 3=blue, 4=red\n- Pets: 1=fish, 2=bird, 3=cat, 4=dog\n\n1. Ivy (3) and Kim (4) next door \u2713\n2. Jon (2) immediately left of blue (3) \u2713\n3. Red (4) right of Leo (1) \u2713\n4. Leo (1) not in green (2) \u2713\n5. Kim (4) at least 2 from green (2): |4-2|=2 \u2713\n6. Dog (4) at least 2 from Jon (2): |4-2|=2 \u2713\n7. Fish (1) immediately left of Jon (2) \u2713\n8. Bird (2) next door to Ivy (3) \u2713\n\nAll constraints satisfied!\n\nLet me quickly check Case 2 to make sure there's no other solution.\n\n**Case 2: Jon in house 3, Fish in house 2, Blue in house 4**\n\nDog at least 2 from Jon (3): dog in house 1 (|1-3|=2). So dog in house 1.\n\nPets: House 1: Dog, House 2: Fish, Houses 3,4: cat, bird.\n\nBird next door to Ivy. Ivy and Kim adjacent.\n\nOwners: Jon in 3. Ivy, Kim, Leo in 1,2,4. Ivy and Kim adjacent: possible (1,2) or... (2,?) - 2 adjacent to 1,3. 3 is Jon. So (1,2) or (4,?) - 4 adjacent to 3 only. So Ivy, Kim in 1,2. Leo in 4.\n\nLeo in 4. Red to the right of Leo? No house to the right of 4. Contradiction!\n\nSo Case 2 is imp"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-015", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Drawing all three marble colors", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 7803, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 909, "reasoning_tokens": 729, "input_tokens": 79, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 417, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2231, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "4/7", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "4/7"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje62d6dba-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje53499c2-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:48-0500", "answer": "Total ways to draw 4 marbles from 9:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{9}{4}=126\n\\]\n\nFavorable cases where all three colors appear:\n\n- 2 red, 1 blue, 1 green: \\(\\binom{4}{2}\\binom{3}{1}\\binom{2}{1}=36\\)\n- 1 red, 2 blue, 1 green: \\(\\binom{4}{1}\\binom{3}{2}\\binom{2}{1}=24\\)\n- 1 red, 1 blue, 2 green: \\(\\binom{4}{1}\\binom{3}{1}\\binom{2}{2}=12\\)\n\nTotal favorable:\n\n\\[\n36+24+12=72\n\\]\n\nProbability:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{72}{126}=\\frac{4}{7}\n\\]\n\nANSWER: 4/7"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-010", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Shift-and-xor hash trace", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 8744, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 568, "reasoning_tokens": 290, "input_tokens": 102, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 542, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "45578", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "45578"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje696d66f-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje53472af-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:49-0500", "answer": "Starting with `x = 0`, each iteration computes the new value and keeps only its low 16 bits:\n\n| `i` | `ch` | `ord(ch) * (i + 1)` | New `x` (hex) |\n|---:|:---:|---:|---:|\n| 0 | `o` | 111 | `0x006F` |\n| 1 | `r` | 228 | `0x0D09` |\n| 2 | `k` | 321 | `0xA1C0` |\n| 3 | `e` | 404 | `0x2DAC` |\n| 4 | `s` | 575 | `0xB20A` |\n\nFor example, the last iteration is:\n```text\n((0x2DAC << 5) ^ (0x2DAC >> 3) ^ 0x023F) & 0xFFFF\n= (0x5B580 ^ 0x05B5 ^ 0x023F) & 0xFFFF\n= 0xB20A\n```\n\n`0xB20A` is `45578` in decimal, which is what `print(x)` prints.\n\nANSWER: 45578"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-009", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Round-robin scheduler with arrivals", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 11940, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1845, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 251, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 3806, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "b:9,d:11,a:16,c:18,e:20", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "b:9,d:11,a:16,c:18,e:20"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje5600b58-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje5344b9d-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:51-0500", "answer": "I need to trace this round-robin scheduling simulation step by step.\n\n**Initial state:**\n- arrivals = deque([(0, \"a\", 5), (1, \"b\", 3), (2, \"c\", 6), (6, \"d\", 2), (7, \"e\", 4)])\n- quantum = 2, clock = 0, ready = deque(), done = []\n\n**First admit() call (clock = 0):**\n- arrivals[0] = (0, \"a\", 5), 0 <= 0, so pop: ready = [[\"a\", 5]]\n- arrivals[0] = (1, \"b\", 3), 1 <= 0? No. Stop.\n- arrivals = deque([(1, \"b\", 3), (2, \"c\", 6), (6, \"d\", 2), (7, \"e\", 4)])\n\n**Main loop iteration 1:**\n- ready = [[\"a\", 5]], not empty\n- job = [\"a\", 5], ready = []\n- run = min(2, 5) = 2, clock = 0 + 2 = 2\n- job[1] = 5 - 2 = 3\n- admit() with clock = 2:\n  - (1, \"b\", 3): 1 <= 2, pop, ready = [[\"b\", 3]]\n  - (2, \"c\", 6): 2 <= 2, pop, ready = [[\"b\", 3], [\"c\", 6]]\n  - (6, \"d\", 2): 6 <= 2? No. Stop.\n  - arrivals = deque([(6, \"d\", 2), (7, \"e\", 4)])\n- job[1] = 3 (truthy), so ready.append([\"a\", 3])\n- ready = [[\"b\", 3], [\"c\", 6], [\"a\", 3]]\n\n**Main loop iteration 2:**\n- job = [\"b\", 3], ready = [[\"c\", 6], [\"a\", 3]]\n- run = min(2, 3) = 2, clock = 2 + 2 = 4\n- job[1] = 3 - 2 = 1\n- admit() with clock = 4:\n  - (6, \"d\", 2): 6 <= 4? No. Nothing admitted.\n- job[1] = 1 (truthy), ready.append([\"b\", 1])\n- ready = [[\"c\", 6], [\"a\", 3], [\"b\", 1]]\n\n**Main loop iteration 3:**\n- job = [\"c\", 6], ready = [[\"a\", 3], [\"b\", 1]]\n- run = min(2, 6) = 2, clock = 4 + 2 = 6\n- job[1] = 6 - 2 = 4\n- admit() with clock = 6:\n  - (6, \"d\", 2): 6 <= 6, pop, ready = [[\"a\", 3], [\"b\", 1], [\"d\", 2]]\n  - (7, \"e\", 4): 7 <= 6? No. Stop.\n  - arrivals = deque([(7, \"e\", 4)])\n- job[1] = 4 (truthy), ready.append([\"c\", 4])\n- ready = [[\"a\", 3], [\"b\", 1], [\"d\", 2], [\"c\", 4]]\n\n**Main loop iteration 4:**\n- job = [\"a\", 3], ready = [[\"b\", 1], [\"d\", 2], [\"c\", 4]]\n- run = min(2, 3) = 2, clock = 6 + 2 = 8\n- job[1] = 3 - 2 = 1\n- admit() with clock = 8:\n  - (7, \"e\", 4): 7 <= 8, pop, ready = [[\"b\", 1], [\"d\", 2], [\"c\", 4], [\"e\", 4]]\n  - arrivals = deque() (empty)\n- job[1] = 1 (truthy), ready.append([\"a\", 1])\n- ready = [[\"b\", 1], [\"d\", 2], [\"c\", 4], [\"e\", 4], [\"a\", 1]]\n\n**Main loop iteration 5:**\n- job = [\"b\", 1], ready = [[\"d\", 2], [\"c\", 4], [\"e\", 4], [\"a\", 1]]\n- run = min(2, 1) = 1, clock = 8 + 1 = 9\n- job[1] = 1 - 1 = 0\n- admit() with clock = 9: arrivals empty, nothing happens\n- job[1] = 0 (falsy), done.append(\"b:9\")\n- done = [\"b:9\"]\n\n**Main loop iteration 6:**\n- job = [\"d\", 2], ready = [[\"c\", 4], [\"e\", 4], [\"a\", 1]]\n- run = min(2, 2) = 2, clock = 9 + 2 = 11\n- job[1] = 2 - 2 = 0\n- admit(): nothing\n- job[1] = 0, done.append(\"d:11\")\n- done = [\"b:9\", \"d:11\"]\n\n**Main loop iteration 7:**\n- job = [\"c\", 4], ready = [[\"e\", 4], [\"a\", 1]]\n- run = min(2, 4) = 2, clock = 11 + 2 = 13\n- job[1] = 4 - 2 = 2\n- admit(): nothing\n- job[1] = 2 (truthy), ready.append([\"c\", 2])\n- ready = [[\"e\", 4], [\"a\", 1], [\"c\", 2]]\n\n**Main loop iteration 8:**\n- job = [\"e\", 4], ready = [[\"a\", 1], [\"c\", 2]]\n- run = min(2, 4) = 2, clock = 13 + 2 = 15\n- job[1] = 4 - 2 = 2\n- admit(): nothing\n- job[1] = 2 (truthy), ready.append([\"e\", 2])\n- ready = [[\"a\", 1], [\"c\", 2], [\"e\", 2]]\n\n**Main loop iteration 9:**\n- job = [\"a\", 1], ready = [[\"c\", 2], [\"e\", 2]]\n- run = min(2, 1) = 1, clock = 15 + 1 = 16\n- job[1] = 1 - 1 = 0\n- admit(): nothing\n- job[1] = 0, done.append(\"a:16\")\n- done = [\"b:9\", \"d:11\", \"a:16\"]\n\n**Main loop iteration 10:**\n- job = [\"c\", 2], ready = [[\"e\", 2]]\n- run = min(2, 2) = 2, clock = 16 + 2 = 18\n- job[1] = 2 - 2 = 0\n- admit(): nothing\n- job[1] = 0, done.append(\"c:18\")\n- done = [\"b:9\", \"d:11\", \"a:16\", \"c:18\"]\n\n**Main loop iteration 11:**\n- job = [\"e\", 2], ready = []\n- run = min(2, 2) = 2, clock = 18 + 2 = 20\n- job[1] = 2 - 2 = 0\n- admit(): nothing\n- job[1] = 0, done.append(\"e:20\")\n- done = [\"b:9\", \"d:11\", \"a:16\", \"c:18\", \"e:20\"]\n\n**Loop ends:** ready is empty and arrivals is empty.\n\n**Final print:** `\",\".join(done)` = \"b:9,d:11,a:16,c:18,e:20\"\n\nANSWER: b:9,d:11,a:16,c:18,e:20"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "reasoning-016", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Four houses: owners and pets", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 11863, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 683, "reasoning_tokens": 500, "input_tokens": 236, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 586, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "Leo, Jon, Ivy, Kim, fish, bird, cat, dog", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "Leo, Jon, Ivy, Kim, fish, bird, cat, dog"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje59b8dd5-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfje53499c1-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:09:51-0500", "answer": "Jon must live in house 2 or 3, with the fish to his left and the blue house to his right. If Jon lived in house 3, Ivy and Kim would occupy houses 1 and 2, leaving Leo in house 4\u2014with no room for the red house to his right.\n\nThus Jon is in house 2, Leo in house 1, and Ivy and Kim in houses 3 and 4. Kim cannot occupy house 3: that would force the green house to be Leo\u2019s. So Ivy is in house 3 and Kim in house 4.\n\nThe fish is in house 1, the dog in house 4, and the bird must be in house 2 next to Ivy. The cat is therefore in house 3.\n\nANSWER: Leo, Jon, Ivy, Kim, fish, bird, cat, dog"}
