{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "grounding-003", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Literature and Peace laureates", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 11348, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 6, "output_tokens": 869, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 802, "search_tokens": 26989, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 2330, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navi Pillay", "expected": "Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navi Pillay", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 8}, "workflow_id": "0sfj2747a8d0-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj26499942-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:25:59-0500", "answer": "Based on my web searches, here are the 2026 Nobel Prize winners:\n\n## 2026 Nobel Prize in Literature: **Anne Carson**\n\nThe Swedish Academy announced on **8 October 2026** that the Canadian poet, essayist, classicist, and translator **Anne Carson** won the 2026 Nobel Prize in Literature \"for her bold and inventive oeuvre that, in playful dialogue with the classical tradition, has created new forms for contemporary literature.\" Carson, 76, is known for genre-blending works such as *Autobiography of Red*, *The Beauty of the Husband*, and *Nox* [1][2][3][4].\n\n## 2026 Nobel Peace Prize: **Navi Pillay**\n\nThe Norwegian Nobel Committee announced on **9 October 2026** that South African jurist **Navanethem \"Navi\" Pillay** won the 2026 Nobel Peace Prize \"for her efforts to promote peace and international law.\" Pillay, 85, is a former UN High Commissioner for Human Rights (2008\u20132014), former judge on the International Criminal Court, and currently serves as an ad hoc judge on the International Court of Justice in the Myanmar genocide case. She is the first South African woman to win the Nobel Peace Prize [5][6][7][8].\n\n---\n\n**Sources:**\n- [1] NobelPrize.org \u2013 Literature 2026 Press Release: https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/literature/2026/press-release/\n- [2] NobelPrize.org \u2013 Literature 2026 Prize Announcement: https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/literature/2026/prize-announcement/\n- [3] Al Jazeera \u2013 \"Canadian Anne Carson wins 2026 Nobel Prize in Literature\": https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/8/canadian-anne-carson-wins-2026-nobel-prize-in-literature\n- [4] PBS News \u2013 \"WATCH: Canadian writer Anne Carson wins Nobel Prize in literature\": https://www.pbs.org/newshour/arts/watch-live-winner-of-the-2026-nobel-prize-in-literature-is\n- [5] NobelPrize.org \u2013 Peace 2026 Press Release: https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/peace/2026/press-release/\n- [6] NobelPrize.org \u2013 Peace 2026 Prize Announcement: https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/peace/2026/prize-announcement/\n- [7] Al Jazeera \u2013 \"2026 Nobel Peace Prize awarded to Navi Pillay\": https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/9/2026-nobel-peace-prize-awarded-to-navi-pillay\n- [8] PBS News \u2013 \"WATCH: Navi Pillay wins Nobel Peace Prize\": https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/watch-live-winner-of-the-2026-nobel-peace-prize-is\n\nANSWER: Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navi Pillay", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
