{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "grounding-004", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 US Open men's singles final", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 14995, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 2, "output_tokens": 1002, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 805, "search_tokens": 12151, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1287, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1907, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Alexander Zverev; Ben Shelton", "expected": "Alexander Zverev; Ben Shelton", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 0}, "workflow_id": "0sfj269d37a3-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj26497230-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:26:02-0500", "answer": "I'll search the web for the 2026 US Open men's singles result.Based on my web search, multiple consistent sources confirm the result of the 2026 US Open men's singles final.\n\n**Result:** Alexander Zverev (Germany) won the men's singles title at the 2026 US Open, defeating American Ben Shelton in the final **6\u20133, 7\u20136(7\u20132), 5\u20137, 6\u20132** on Sunday, September 13, 2026. It was Zverev's second major title of the year (following the 2026 French Open) and the first US Open men's singles title won by a German since Boris Becker in 1989.\n\n**Sources cited:**\n1. Wikipedia \u2013 \"2026 US Open \u2013 Men's singles\" (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_US_Open_%E2%80%93_Men's_singles): \"Alexander Zverev defeated Ben Shelton in the final, 6\u20133, 7\u20136(7\u20132), 5\u20137, 6\u20132 to win the men's singles tennis title at the 2026 US Open.\"\n2. Official US Open website \u2013 \"Alexander Zverev defeats Ben Shelton to win 2026 US Open\" (usopen.org/en_US/news/articles/2026-09-13/...): confirms Zverev as champion over Shelton; the official draw PDF also lists \"Champion: ZVEREV, Alexander GER \u2014 6-3 | 7-6(2) | 5-7 | 6-2\".\n3. ATP Tour \u2013 \"What were the US Open results?\" (atptour.com/en/news/us-open-2026-results): \"The US Open concluded on Sunday, when Alexander Zverev won the men's singles title.\"\n\nANSWER: Alexander Zverev; Ben Shelton", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "grounding-004", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 US Open men's singles final", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 15686, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 6, "output_tokens": 583, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 805, "search_tokens": 42060, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1319, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Alexander Zverev; Ben Shelton", "expected": "Alexander Zverev; Ben Shelton", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 0}, "workflow_id": "0sfj269d37a4-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj26497230-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:26:03-0500", "answer": "Based on my web searches, I found consistent reporting from multiple authoritative sources about the 2026 US Open men's singles final.\n\n**Alexander Zverev** of Germany won the men's singles title at the 2026 US Open, defeating **Ben Shelton** of the United States in the final with a score of **6\u20133, 7\u20136(7\u20132), 5\u20137, 6\u20132** on Sunday, September 13, 2026, at Arthur Ashe Stadium in New York. It was Zverev's second major title of 2026 (following his French Open win) and his first US Open title \u2014 the first German man to win the US Open since Boris Becker in 1989. Shelton was playing in his first Grand Slam final.\n\n**Sources:**\n- Official US Open website: \"Alexander Zverev defeats Ben Shelton to win 2026 US Open\" (usopen.org, Sept. 13, 2026) and the official 2026 Men's Singles draw PDF listing Zverev as champion\n- ESPN: \"Alexander Zverev beats Ben Shelton in 4 sets to win US Open\" (Sept. 14, 2026)\n- BBC Sport: \"US Open 2026 results: Alexander Zverev beats Ben Shelton for second Grand Slam title\" (Sept. 2026)\n- Associated Press: \"Alexander Zverev beats Ben Shelton to win the US Open title and extend a drought by American men\" (Sept. 13, 2026)\n- ATP Tour: \"What were the US Open results?\" (atptour.com)\n- Wikipedia: \"2026 US Open \u2013 Men's singles\" and \"2026 US Open (tennis)\"\n\nANSWER: Alexander Zverev; Ben Shelton", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "grounding-003", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Literature and Peace laureates", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 15031, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 4, "output_tokens": 968, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 802, "search_tokens": 15114, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1665, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1641, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navi Pillay", "expected": "Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navi Pillay", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 5}, "workflow_id": "0sfj2747a8cd-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj26499942-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:26:04-0500", "answer": "I'll search for the 2026 Nobel Prize winners in Literature and Peace.The searches give clear results. Let me verify with the official Nobel Prize press releases.Both winners are confirmed by the official Nobel Prize press releases, corroborated by news coverage.\n\n**2026 Nobel Prize in Literature \u2014 Anne Carson**\nThe Swedish Academy announced on 8 October 2026 that the Canadian poet, essayist, and classicist Anne Carson won \"for her bold and inventive oeuvre that, in playful dialogue with the classical tradition, has created new forms for contemporary literature\" [NobelPrize.org](https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/literature/2026/press-release/) [Al Jazeera](https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/8/canadian-anne-carson-wins-2026-nobel-prize-in-literature).\n\n**2026 Nobel Peace Prize \u2014 Navi Pillay**\nThe Norwegian Nobel Committee announced on 9 October 2026 that South African jurist Navanethem \"Navi\" Pillay won \"for her efforts to promote peace and international law.\" Pillay, born in Durban in 1941, defended anti-apartheid activists (including Nelson Mandela), served as a judge on the International Criminal Tribunal for Rwanda and the International Criminal Court, was UN High Commissioner for Human Rights (2008\u20132014), and chaired the UN Independent International Commission of Inquiry on the Occupied Palestinian Territory [NobelPrize.org](https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/peace/2026/press-release/) [Al Jazeera](https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/9/2026-nobel-peace-prize-awarded-to-navi-pillay) [PBS/AP](https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/watch-live-winner-of-the-2026-nobel-peace-prize-is).\n\nANSWER: Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navi Pillay", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "grounding-002", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 17752, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 8, "output_tokens": 995, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 807, "search_tokens": 35030, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 2361, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics", "expected": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; optogenetics (light-gated ion channels)", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 6}, "workflow_id": "0sfj26c7f134-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj26497231-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:26:05-0500", "answer": "The 2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine was announced on 5 October 2026 by the Nobel Assembly at Karolinska Institutet. It was awarded jointly to three laureates, each receiving one-third of the prize:\n\n- **Karl Deisseroth** \u2014 Howard Hughes Medical Institute and Stanford University, USA\n- **Peter Hegemann** \u2014 Humboldt University of Berlin, Germany\n- **Georg Nagel** \u2014 University of W\u00fcrzburg, Germany\n\nThe prize recognized **\u201ctheir discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics.\u201d** In essence, the award honored the development of optogenetics \u2014 a revolutionary method that uses light to switch individual nerve cells on or off in the living brain. Hegemann and Nagel discovered the light-sensitive protein channelrhodopsin in the single-celled alga *Chlamydomonas*, and Deisseroth transformed that protein into a light-controlled switch for mammalian neurons, laying the foundation for a new era in neuroscience.\n\n**Sources:**\n- NobelPrize.org \u2014 Press release: [https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/2026/press-release/](https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/2026/press-release/)\n- NobelPrize.org \u2014 Prize summary: [https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/2026/summary/](https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/2026/summary/)\n- Nature \u2014 \u201cMedicine Nobel awarded for brain \u2018switch\u2019 that controls neurons with light\u201d: [https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03091-2](https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03091-2)\n- AP News \u2014 \u201cDeisseroth, Hegemann and Nagel win Nobel Prize in medicine\u201d: [https://apnews.com/article/nobel-prize-medicine-sweden-2efe9ee7eae9d808fd49a6da1f53ceba](https://apnews.com/article/nobel-prize-medicine-sweden-2efe9ee7eae9d808fd49a6da1f53ceba)\n- STAT \u2014 \u201cDeisseroth, Hegemann, Nagel awarded 2026 Nobel Prize in Medicine\u201d: [https://www.statnews.com/2026/10/05/nobel-prize-medicine-2026-winner-deisseroth-hegemann-nagel/](https://www.statnews.com/2026/10/05/nobel-prize-medicine-2026-winner-deisseroth-hegemann-nagel/)\n- C&EN \u2014 \u201cOptogenetics researchers win Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine\u201d: [https://cen.acs.org/people/nobel-prize/nobel-2026-physiology-medicine/104/web/2026/10](https://cen.acs.org/people/nobel-prize/nobel-2026-physiology-medicine/104/web/2026/10)\n\nANSWER: Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "grounding-001", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Prize in Physics", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 12448, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 6, "output_tokens": 576, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 802, "search_tokens": 31635, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1586, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Francis Halzen; IceCube Neutrino Observatory", "expected": "Francis Halzen; IceCube Neutrino Observatory", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 6}, "workflow_id": "0sfj2814f2dc-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2649722f-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:26:05-0500", "answer": "The 2026 Nobel Prize in Physics was awarded to **Francis Halzen** (Belgian-born physicist, professor at the University of Wisconsin\u2013Madison) \u2014 and he is the **sole laureate** this year, the first lone physics laureate since 1992. The official prize citation reads: *\"for decisive contributions to the IceCube Neutrino Observatory and the discovery of high-energy neutrinos of astrophysical origin.\"* The observatory at the heart of the citation is the **IceCube Neutrino Observatory** at the South Pole \u2014 a cubic-kilometre neutrino detector embedded ~2 km deep in the Antarctic ice, equipped with light sensors that detect neutrinos from the distant cosmos.\n\n**Sources:**\n- NobelPrize.org \u2013 Press release: Nobel Prize in Physics 2026 \u2014 https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/physics/2026/press-release/\n- NobelPrize.org \u2013 Francis Halzen Facts \u2013 https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/physics/2026/halzen/facts/\n- AIP \u2013 \"Francis Halzen and the anatomy of a solo Nobel Prize\" \u2013 https://www.aip.org/history/halzen-solo-nobel\n- Physics World \u2013 \"Francis Halzen wins Nobel Prize in Physics\" \u2013 https://physicsworld.com/a/francis-halzen-wins-nobel-prize-in-physics/\n- Scientific American \u2013 \"2026 Nobel Prize in Physics awarded to Francis Halzen...\" \u2013 https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/2026-nobel-prize-in-physics-awarded-to-francis-halzen-for-discovery-of-high-energy-neutrinos/\n- NPR \u2013 \"Francis Halzen wins Nobel Prize in physics for work on high-energy neutrinos from space\" \u2013 https://www.npr.org/2026/10/06/g-s1-146622/nobel-prize-physics\n\nANSWER: Francis Halzen; IceCube Neutrino Observatory", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "grounding-002", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 18627, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 3, "output_tokens": 1187, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 807, "search_tokens": 20327, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1952, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2507, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics", "expected": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; optogenetics (light-gated ion channels)", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 5}, "workflow_id": "0sfj26c81845-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj26497231-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:26:06-0500", "answer": "I'll search for the 2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine laureates.The search results are consistent. Let me verify against the official Nobel Prize press release for the exact citation.The 2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine was announced on 5 October 2026 by the Nobel Assembly at Karolinska Institutet. It was awarded jointly to three laureates:\n\n- **Karl Deisseroth** \u2014 Howard Hughes Medical Institute and Stanford University, USA\n- **Peter Hegemann** \u2014 Humboldt University of Berlin, Germany\n- **Georg Nagel** \u2014 University of W\u00fcrzburg, Germany\n\nThe official citation reads: *\"for their discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics.\"* The research area recognized is **optogenetics** \u2014 the technique of using light to control nerve-cell activity. Hegemann and Nagel discovered the light-sensitive algal protein channelrhodopsin in the single-celled alga *Chlamydomonas*, and Deisseroth turned it into a light-controlled switch for neurons, enabling precise control of nerve cells in the living brain and laying the foundation for a new era in neuroscience. The prize amount was 12 million Swedish kronor, shared equally among the three laureates.\n\n**Sources:**\n- NobelPrize.org, official press release (5 October 2026): https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/2026/press-release/\n- NobelPrize.org, prize summary: https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/2026/summary/\n- C&EN (Chemical & Engineering News), \"Optogenetics researchers win Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine\": https://cen.acs.org/people/nobel-prize/nobel-2026-physiology-medicine/104/web/2026/10\n- TIME, \"Meet the 2026 Nobel Prize Winners\": https://time.com/article/2026/10/05/nobel-prize-2026-winners/\n- Wikipedia, \"Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine\": https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nobel_Prize_in_Physiology_or_Medicine\n\nANSWER: Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
