{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "grounding-001", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Prize in Physics", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 22232, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 4, "output_tokens": 1087, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 802, "search_tokens": 12387, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1830, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1972, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Francis Halzen; IceCube Neutrino Observatory", "expected": "Francis Halzen; IceCube Neutrino Observatory", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 4}, "workflow_id": "0sfj2814cbc9-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2649722f-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:26:15-0500", "answer": "The search results are consistent. Let me verify with the official Nobel Prize press release.The 2026 Nobel Prize in Physics was announced on **6 October 2026** by the Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences. It was awarded to a single laureate:\n\n- **Francis Halzen** (born 1944 in Tienen, Belgium; Professor at the University of Wisconsin\u2013Madison, USA)\n- **Prize citation:** *\"for decisive contributions to the IceCube Neutrino Observatory and the discovery of high-energy neutrinos of astrophysical origin\"*\n\nThe citation is built around the **IceCube Neutrino Observatory** \u2014 a cubic-kilometre neutrino detector embedded in the glacial ice at the South Pole in Antarctica. Halzen first proposed the idea in 1988; the observatory was completed in 2011 and has since captured high-energy astrophysical neutrinos, opening a new window on the universe.\n\n**Sources:**\n1. NobelPrize.org \u2014 Official press release, \"Nobel Prize in Physics 2026\" (6 October 2026): https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/physics/2026/press-release/ [search-result://Qx9ylYCB, search-result://11InOaIf, search-result://l35NcRsl]\n2. PBS News \u2014 \"Nobel Prize in physics awarded to Francis Halzen for demystifying neutrinos\" (6 October 2026): https://www.pbs.org/newshour/science/watch-live-winner-of-the-2026-nobel-prize-in-physics-is [search-result://CIRJ7zNV]\n3. Scientific American \u2014 \"2026 Nobel Prize in Physics awarded to Francis Halzen for discovery of high-energy neutrinos\": https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/2026-nobel-prize-in-physics-awarded-to-francis-halzen-for-discovery-of-high-energy-neutrinos/ [search-result://zPenUI6Z]\n4. AIP \u2014 \"AIP Congratulates 2026 Nobel Prize Winner in Physics\": https://www.aip.org/aip/aip-congratulates-2026-nobel-prize-winner-in-physics [search-result://4V3yAdHf]\n\nANSWER: Francis Halzen; IceCube Neutrino Observatory", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
