{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "grounding-011", "category": "grounding", "title": "US 2025 median household income and poverty rate", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4887, "turns": 1, "retries": 1, "usage": {"search_calls": 2, "output_tokens": 183, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 848, "search_tokens": 13912, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 244, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "$87,460; 10.2%", "expected": "$87,460; 10.2%", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 5}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6a4bcb12-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj64cf2093-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:28:06-0500", "answer": "According to the U.S. Census Bureau's income and poverty report released in September 2026, the real median household income in the United States for 2025 was **$87,460**. The official poverty rate in 2025 was **10.2%**.\n\nANSWER: $87,460; 10.2%", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "grounding-011", "category": "grounding", "title": "US 2025 median household income and poverty rate", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 12702, "turns": 1, "retries": 1, "usage": {"search_calls": 6, "output_tokens": 536, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 822, "search_tokens": 23913, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1139, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "$87,460; 10.2%", "expected": "$87,460; 10.2%", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 3}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6a4b7cef-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj64cf2093-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:28:14-0500", "answer": "According to the U.S. Census Bureau's reports released on **September 15, 2026** (based on the 2026 Current Population Survey Annual Social and Economic Supplement, covering calendar year 2025):\n\n- **Real median household income in 2025:** **$87,460** \u2014 an increase of 2.6% from the 2024 estimate of $85,210, and the highest on record dating back to 1967. [Source: Census Bureau press release CB26-151](https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/income-poverty-health-insurance-coverage.html); [Income in the United States: 2025 (P60-289)](https://www.census.gov/library/publications/2026/demo/p60-289.html)\n\n- **Official poverty rate in 2025:** **10.2%** \u2014 down 0.5 percentage points from 2024, with 34.5 million people in poverty. [Source: Census Bureau press release CB26-151](https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/income-poverty-health-insurance-coverage.html); [Poverty in the United States: 2025 (P60-290)](https://www.census.gov/library/publications/2026/demo/p60-290.html)\n\n(For context, the Supplemental Poverty Measure rate was 13.1% in 2025, not statistically different from 2024.)\n\nANSWER: $87,460; 10.2%", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "grounding-011", "category": "grounding", "title": "US 2025 median household income and poverty rate", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 13925, "turns": 1, "retries": 1, "usage": {"search_calls": 4, "output_tokens": 1484, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 822, "search_tokens": 20384, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1872, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2955, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "$87,460; 10.2%", "expected": "$87,460; 10.2%", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 4}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6a4ba400-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj64cf2093-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:28:15-0500", "answer": "I'll search for the Census Bureau's September 2026 income and poverty report covering 2025 data.The search results are consistent across the Census Bureau and multiple news outlets. Let me verify directly against the Census Bureau's official press release.According to the U.S. Census Bureau's press release (CB26-151) issued **September 15, 2026**, titled \"Income, Poverty and Health Insurance Coverage in the United States: 2025,\" which draws on the 2026 Current Population Survey Annual Social and Economic Supplement (CPS ASEC):\n\n- **Real median household income in 2025 was $87,460** \u2014 an increase of 2.6% from the 2024 estimate of $85,210, and the highest on record dating back to 1967.\n- **The official poverty rate in 2025 was 10.2%** \u2014 down 0.5 percentage points from 2024, with 34.5 million people in poverty. (For context, the Supplemental Poverty Measure rate was 13.1%, not statistically different from 2024.)\n\nThese figures are drawn from the Census Bureau's companion reports \"Income in the United States: 2025\" (P60-289) and \"Poverty in the United States: 2025\" (P60-290), and are corroborated by contemporaneous news coverage.\n\n**Sources:**\n1. U.S. Census Bureau, Press Release CB26-151, \"Income, Poverty and Health Insurance Coverage in the United States: 2025,\" Sept. 15, 2026 \u2014 https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/income-poverty-health-insurance-coverage.html\n2. U.S. Census Bureau, \"Income in the United States: 2025\" (P60-289) \u2014 https://www.census.gov/library/publications/2026/demo/p60-289.html\n3. U.S. Census Bureau, \"Poverty in the United States: 2025\" (P60-290) \u2014 https://www.census.gov/library/publications/2026/demo/p60-290.html\n4. CNBC, \"Americans' incomes rose and poverty fell in 2025, Census Bureau says,\" Sept. 15, 2026 \u2014 https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/15/income-poverty-census-fed-interest-rates.html\n\nANSWER: $87,460; 10.2%", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
