s published on September 25, 2026, which is before October 20, 2026.\n\n**Sources:**\n1. [GitHub Releases page - conductor-oss/conductor](https://github.com/conductor-oss/conductor/releases) \u2014 shows v3.32.5 marked as \"Latest\" and all v3.33.0-rc* as \"Pre-release\"\n2. [Release v3.32.5 - conductor-oss/conductor](https://github.com/conductor-oss/conductor/releases/tag/v3.32.5) \u2014 confirms the stable release tag and date (Sep 25, 2026)\n\nANSWER: v3.32.5", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "grounding-006", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Asian Games medal table leader", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 30579, "turns": 1, "retries": 2, "usage": {"search_calls": 9, "output_tokens": 1022, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 814, "search_tokens": 53061, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 2447, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "China; 169", "expected": "China; 169", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 7}, "workflow_id": "0sfj66979746-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj64cf2090-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:06-0500", "answer": "Based on my web searches, I found consistent reporting across multiple sources about the final medal standings at the 2026 Asian Games in Aichi-Nagoya, Japan.\n\n**Key findings:**\n\nThe 20th Asian Games (Aichi-Nagoya 2026) were held from 19 September to 4 October 2026, featuring 469 events across 43 sports. Multiple independent sources confirm the final medal table results:\n\n- **Xinhua News Agency** (China's official state news agency) reported: \"The Aichi-Nagoya Asian Games came to a close Sunday, with China topping the gold medal table for the 12th consecutive edition, and finishing with **169 gold, 89 silver and 83 bronze medals**, its best haul at an overseas Asiad.\" [Source: english.news.cn](https://english.news.cn/20261004/0d5d63d5f50a41a28f9cf40229426dcf/c.html)\n\n- **The Mainichi** (Japanese newspaper/Kyodo News) reported: \"China finished comfortably atop the medal standings with **341 medals, including 169 golds**\" [Source: mainichi.jp](https://mainichi.jp/english/articles/20261005/p2g00m0sp002000c)\n\n- **Times of India** medal tally page confirmed: \"China: **169 Gold** | 89 Silver | 83 Bronze | Total: 341\" [Source: timesofindia.indiatimes.com](https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/asian-games/medal-tally)\n\n- **Khel Now** reported: \"China topped the final medal standings with **169 gold**, 89 silver and 83 bronze medals, for a total of 341 medals.\" [Source: khelnow.com](https://khelnow.com/asian-games/final-medal-tally-asian-games-202610)\n\n- **Indian Express** analysis confirmed: \"China conquered the Asian Games in Aichi-Nagoya, claiming a whopping 341 medals, **169 of them gold**.\" [Source: indianexpress.com](https://indianexpress.com/article/sports/china-japan-biggest-winner-asian-games-2026-medal-tally-analysis-10906462/)\n\n- **Wikipedia's 2026 Asian Games medal table** shows China ranked #1 with 169 gold, 89 silver, 83 bronze (341 total) [Source: en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Asian_Games_medal_table](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Asian_Games_medal_table)\n\n- **Olympics.com** (International Olympic Committee's official platform) has the final medal table for Aichi-Nagoya 2026 [Source: olympics.com](https://www.olympics.com/en/news/20th-asian-games-aichi-nagoya-2026-medal-table-live-updates)\n\nChina topped the medal table for the **12th consecutive Asian Games** (since 1982), finishing well ahead of host nation Japan (83 gold, 269 total) and South Korea (39 gold, 150 total).\n\nANSWER: China; 169", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "grounding-012", "category": "grounding", "title": "Mistral Large 4 announcement and size", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 36149, "turns": 1, "retries": 2, "usage": {"search_calls": 6, "output_tokens": 3276, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 813, "search_tokens": 28397, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 2643, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 10201, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "2026-10-06; 1 trillion total; 52 billion active", "expected": "2026-10-06; 1 trillion total; 52 billion active", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 3}, "workflow_id": "0sfj64f66a37-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj64cf2091-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:10-0500", "answer": "I'll search for the announcement details of Mistral Large 4.I found the announcement date (October 6, 2026), but there's a discrepancy in reported active parameters (49B vs 52B) between the announcement and docs, and some sources say the announcement was later updated. Since the question specifically asks what **Mistral's announcement** says, let me open the official announcement to get the exact wording.The official announcement is at mistral.ai/news/mistral-large-4. The search snippet from Mistral's own page says \"1 trillion-parameter natively multimodal model with **52 billion** active parameters,\" while some secondary sources say the announcement originally said 49B and was later updated. Let me open the official announcement and the model docs to confirm the exact current wording.I now have the authoritative primary sources directly from Mistral.\n\n**What Mistral's announcement says**\n\nMistral's official announcement, **\"Introducing Mistral Large 4\"** (mistral.ai/news/mistral-large-4/), is dated **October 6, 2026** and opens: *\"Today, we're launching a public preview of Mistral Large 4.\"* The key spec line reads:\n\n> *\"ML4 is a **1 trillion-parameter** natively multimodal model with **52 billion active parameters**.\"* [1]\n\nMistral's model documentation/model card for **Mistral Large 4** (docs.mistral.ai/models/mistral-large-4, dated October 6, 2026, \"Public Preview v26.10\") gives the more precise figures: *\"It features **52B active parameters** and **1.05T total parameters**, and a 1.6B vision encoder.\"* [2] So the announcement rounds the total to \"1 trillion,\" while the docs specify 1.05T.\n\n**Note on the 49B vs 52B discrepancy:** Early launch-day coverage (and the announcement's original wording on Oct 6) cited **49B active**, which refers to active *experts* only; Mistral subsequently updated the announcement/model card to the inclusive **52B active** figure (active experts plus embeddings and output layers). The current official announcement text says **52 billion active**. [1][3]\n\n**Sources**\n- [1] Mistral AI \u2014 \"Introducing Mistral Large 4,\" Oct 6, 2026 \u2014 https://mistral.ai/news/mistral-large-4/ (\"1 trillion-parameter \u2026 52 billion active parameters\")\n- [2] Mistral Docs \u2014 \"Mistral Large 4\" model card, Oct 6, 2026 \u2014 https://docs.mistral.ai/models/mistral-large-4 (\"52B active \u2026 1.05T total \u2026 1.6B vision encoder\")\n- [3] Kingy AI \u2014 \"Mistral Large 4: Specs, Benchmarks, Pricing & Comparisons\" \u2014 https://kingy.ai/blog/mistral-large-4-specs-benchmarks-pricing/ (documents the 49B-experts vs 52B-inclusive distinction and the announcement update)\n\nANSWER: 2026-10-06; 1 trillion total; 52 billion active", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-007", "category": "your_data", "title": "Postmortem draft vs customer RCA deadlines", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1154, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 52, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4079, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4076}, "answer_chars": 216, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 43, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4378, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly states both deadlines measured from resolution and accurately defines business days.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja0520a30-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja03577aa-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:15-0500", "answer": "Measured from resolution:\n- **Internal postmortem draft:** within **3 business days**.\n- **Customer-facing RCA:** within **5 business days** for a SEV-1.\n\nBusiness days exclude weekends and Ferngate company holidays."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-001", "category": "your_data", "title": "SEV-1 status page cadence", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 902, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 36, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4083, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4080}, "answer_chars": 151, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 57, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4336, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4333}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer exactly matches the documented SEV-1 cadence: first update within 20 minutes of declaration, then every 30 minutes until resolved.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja1043977-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja0355094-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:16-0500", "answer": "The first status page update is due **within 20 minutes of declaration**. After that, post updates **every 30 minutes until the incident is resolved**."}
