{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-007", "category": "your_data", "title": "Postmortem draft vs customer RCA deadlines", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2573, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 68, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4136, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 279, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 70, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4397, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly states the 3-business-day postmortem draft deadline and 5-business-day SEV-1 customer-facing RCA deadline, both measured from resolution, and accurately includes the optional review meeting deadline.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja051bc0e-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja03577aa-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:17-0500", "answer": "Per the handbook:\n\n- **Internal postmortem draft**: due within **3 business days of resolution** (section 9). The review meeting happens within 7 business days of resolution.\n- **Customer-facing RCA**: published within **5 business days of resolution** for a SEV-1 (section 8.4)."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-004", "category": "your_data", "title": "Security patch during the holiday freeze", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2640, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 110, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4083, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4080}, "answer_chars": 472, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 66, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4486, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies the holiday-freeze exception, requires VP of Engineering approval and progressive rollout, includes timely CAB-register logging, and accurately adds the applicable Normal-change approvals and deploy-window requirements.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja07aa0e0-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja03577a7-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:17-0500", "answer": "Yes. December 22 is within the holiday freeze, but a CVSS 9.3 patch qualifies for the exception for vulnerabilities rated **CVSS 9.0 or higher**.\n\nShip it as a **Normal change** with:\n- **VP of Engineering approval** for the freeze exception.\n- **One approval from the owning team**, plus **CAB approval if the change is high-risk**.\n\nIt must follow the normal deploy windows and progressive rollout. Log the freeze exception in the CAB register within **1 business day**."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-004", "category": "your_data", "title": "Security patch during the holiday freeze", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2913, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 149, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4309, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 606, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 64, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4526, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies the holiday freeze, the CVSS 9.0+ exception allowing a Normal change with VP of Engineering approval, and the progressive rollout and CAB logging requirements.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja07aa0e2-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja03577a7-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:17-0500", "answer": "The document states:\n\n- During the **holiday freeze** (December 18 through January 4), only **Standard and Emergency changes** are allowed.\n- An exception is made for a **security vulnerability rated CVSS 9.0 or higher**, which may ship as a **Normal change** with approval from the **VP of Engineering**.\n- The patch must still follow the **progressive rollout** rules (section 7.3).\n- The exception must be logged in the **CAB register within 1 business day**.\n\nSince the vulnerability is CVSS 9.3 (\u2265 9.0), you may ship the patch on December 22 as a **Normal change** with **VP of Engineering approval**."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-004", "category": "your_data", "title": "Security patch during the holiday freeze", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4023, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 294, "reasoning_tokens": 173, "input_tokens": 4083, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4080}, "answer_chars": 509, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 65, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4491, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies the holiday-freeze security exception, required VP approval, Normal-change requirements, progressive rollout, and CAB-register logging deadline, with all additional requirements supported by the handbook.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja07aa0e3-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja03577a7-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:19-0500", "answer": "**Yes.** December 22 falls within the holiday freeze, but a CVSS 9.3 patch qualifies for the security exception (\u00a77.4).\n\nShip it as a **Normal change**, requiring:\n- **VP of Engineering approval** for the freeze exception.\n- The usual **owning-team approval**.\n- **CAB approval** if it involves a schema migration, network/ACL change, or authentication change.\n\nThe patch must follow the progressive rollout and applicable deploy window. Log the freeze exception in the CAB register within **1 business day**."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-008", "category": "your_data", "title": "Friday deploy with the standard canary", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2465, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 123, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4083, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4080}, "answer_chars": 424, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 86, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4517, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 4, "reason": "The answer correctly rejects 15:00 and calculates the 90-minute rollout, but gives a start strictly before 14:30 rather than the rubric\u2019s required 14:30, although its stricter interpretation is supported by the document\u2019s wording 'before 16:00 UTC'.", "correct": false, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja1102a3a-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja03577a9-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:19-0500", "answer": "No. Friday deploys must reach **100% of traffic before 16:00 UTC**. A Normal rollout requires 30 minutes at 5%, then 60 minutes at 25%\u201490 minutes before reaching 100%.\n\nStarting at 15:00 would reach 100% at 16:30. You must start **before 14:30 UTC**; exactly 14:30 would reach 100% at 16:00, not before it. Friday deploys may start no earlier than 14:00 UTC, and any applicable approvals and freeze restrictions still apply."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-008", "category": "your_data", "title": "Friday deploy with the standard canary", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2999, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 184, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4312, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4224}, "answer_chars": 605, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 89, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4560, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": ["16:30"], "pass": false}, "judge": {"score": 4, "reason": "The answer correctly rejects the 15:00 Normal deploy and gives the reference's 14:30 latest start, but adds an unsupported guarantee about Standard change completion.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": ["A Standard change started at 15:00 UTC would finish on time; the document provides no duration or guaranteed completion time for Standard changes."], "faithful": false}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja110514e-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja03577a9-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:19-0500", "answer": "The document states:\n\n- **Friday**: production deploys may start from **14:00 UTC**, and the change must reach **100% of traffic before 16:00 UTC**.\n- **Progressive rollout** (for Normal changes) takes at least **90 minutes** (30 min canary + 60 min 25% stage).\n\nSince your deploy is a **Normal change**, starting at **15:00 UTC** would not allow completion by **16:00 UTC**. The latest you could start is **14:30 UTC** to finish by **16:00 UTC**.\n\nIf this is a **Standard change** (pre-approved, low-risk), it skips the canary stages, so you could start as late as **15:00 UTC** and still finish on time."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-003", "category": "your_data", "title": "Platinum downtime budget", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2357, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 118, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4312, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4224}, "answer_chars": 359, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 72, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4461, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly calculates 21.6 minutes of downtime from Platinum's 99.95% commitment and states the documented 10% credit, rising to 25% when uptime falls below 99.0%.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja16a365a-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja0355093-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:19-0500", "answer": "For a Platinum customer with a 99.95% monthly uptime commitment in a 30-day month (43,200 minutes), the allowed downtime before owing a service credit is **21.6 minutes** (43,200 \u00d7 0.0005).\n\nIf monthly uptime falls below 99.95%, the service credit is **10% of that month's fees**. If it falls below 99.0%, the credit increases to **25% of that month's fees**."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-003", "category": "your_data", "title": "Platinum downtime budget", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2451, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 130, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4085, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4082}, "answer_chars": 528, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 61, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4491, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly calculates 21.6 minutes of allowed downtime, states the 10% and 25% credit thresholds, and includes only document-supported additional conditions.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja16a0f48-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja0355093-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:19-0500", "answer": "For a Platinum customer, the monthly API uptime commitment is **99.95%**. In a 30-day month (43,200 minutes), that allows **21.6 minutes of downtime**. More downtime puts uptime below the commitment.\n\nThe service credit is:\n- **10% of that month\u2019s fees** if uptime falls below 99.95%.\n- **25% of that month\u2019s fees** if uptime falls below 99.0%\u2014more than 432 minutes of downtime.\n\nCustomers must request credits within **30 days after the affected month ends**. A signed customer contract overrides the handbook if they conflict."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-001", "category": "your_data", "title": "SEV-1 status page cadence", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4038, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 326, "reasoning_tokens": 234, "input_tokens": 4139, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 395, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1058, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 61, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4395, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer gives the required 20-minute initial deadline and 30-minute update cadence until resolution, and its additional communication details are supported by section 8.1.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja1043978-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja0355094-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:19-0500", "answer": "Per section 2.1 of the handbook, for a **SEV-1**:\n\n- **First status page update**: within **20 minutes** of declaration\n- **Subsequent updates**: every **30 minutes** until resolved\n\n(Section 8.1 notes that these updates are written by the Communications Lead and should say what is affected, what customers should expect, and when the next update will come\u2014without naming individual customers.)"}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-003", "category": "your_data", "title": "Platinum downtime budget", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3006, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 196, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4143, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4076}, "answer_chars": 697, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 60, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4557, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly calculates 21.6 minutes of allowed downtime in a 30-day month and states the supported credit amounts, thresholds, and request-processing requirements.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja16a0f47-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja0355093-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:19-0500", "answer": "I can answer this from the handbook.\n\n**Platinum uptime commitment:** 99.95% per calendar month (section 8.2).\n\n**Downtime allowed in a 30-day month before a credit is owed:**\n- 30 days = 43,200 minutes\n- Allowed downtime = 0.05% \u00d7 43,200 = **21.6 minutes** (about 21 minutes 36 seconds)\n\nSo more than ~21.6 minutes of API downtime in a month puts a Platinum customer below their commitment.\n\n**Credit if missed (section 8.3):**\n- Below 99.95% but at or above 99.0%: **10% of that month's fees**\n- Below 99.0%: **25% of that month's fees**\n\nNote: the customer must request the credit within 30 days of the end of the affected month, and Customer Success processes requests within 10 business days."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-007", "category": "your_data", "title": "Postmortem draft vs customer RCA deadlines", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5294, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 426, "reasoning_tokens": 358, "input_tokens": 4136, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 257, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1455, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 68, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4395, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly states the SEV-1 postmortem draft deadline of 3 business days and customer-facing RCA deadline of 5 business days from resolution, with all claims supported by the handbook.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja051e31f-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja03577aa-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:19-0500", "answer": "Based on the handbook:\n\n- **Internal postmortem draft**: Due within **3 business days** of resolution (Section 9). A postmortem is required for every SEV-1.\n- **Customer-facing RCA**: Must be published within **5 business days** of resolution (Section 8.4)."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-004", "category": "your_data", "title": "Security patch during the holiday freeze", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4222, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 265, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4139, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 1026, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 139, "reasoning_tokens": 27, "input_tokens": 4635, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 4, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies the freeze exception, VP approval, progressive rollout, and logging deadline, but makes an unsupported assumption about the patch's risk category.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": ["The answer asserts that the patch is not a high-risk change, although the question does not specify whether it involves schema, network/ACL, or authentication changes."], "faithful": false}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja07aa0df-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja03577a7-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:20-0500", "answer": "Yes, you can ship it on December 22. December 18 through January 4 is the holiday freeze, during which only Standard and Emergency changes are normally allowed \u2014 **but** there's an explicit exception: a patch for a security vulnerability rated **CVSS 9.0 or higher** may ship as a **Normal change** with approval from the **VP of Engineering**.\n\nSince this is CVSS 9.3, it qualifies for the exception. Requirements:\n\n- **Approval:** VP of Engineering (Tobias Renwick)\n- **Change class:** Normal (not Standard or Emergency)\n- **Rollout:** It still follows the progressive rollout in section 7.3 (canary at 5% for 30 min \u2192 25% for 60 min \u2192 100%)\n- **Logging:** The freeze exception must be logged in the **CAB register within 1 business day**\n\nOne note: December 22 falls on a Tuesday in 2026, so if you also need CAB review for the change itself (it's not a high-risk category like a schema migration, network/ACL, or auth change, so CAB may not be required), the CAB meets Tuesdays at 16:00 UTC \u2014 submit by 12:00 UTC that day."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-008", "category": "your_data", "title": "Friday deploy with the standard canary", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3083, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 207, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4141, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4076}, "answer_chars": 706, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 140, "reasoning_tokens": 23, "input_tokens": 4596, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 3, "reason": "The answer correctly calculates the 16:30 completion and gives the reference's latest start of 14:30, but contradicts its own conclusion by initially saying the 15:00 start is allowed.", "correct": false, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": ["The opening claim that a 15:00 UTC Friday start is allowed contradicts the Friday deadline and required 90-minute rollout."], "faithful": false}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja1102a3b-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja03577a9-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:20-0500", "answer": "Yes, a 15:00 UTC Friday start is allowed \u2014 but with a condition.\n\nPer section 7.2, on Fridays production deploys may start from 14:00 UTC, **and the change must reach 100% of traffic before 16:00 UTC**.\n\nSince your change is Normal (not Standard), it must go through the progressive rollout in section 7.3:\n1. Canary at 5% for 30 minutes\n2. 25% for 60 minutes\n3. 100%\n\nThat's a minimum of **90 minutes** of rollout stages. Starting at 15:00 UTC means you'd reach 100% at 16:30 UTC \u2014 **30 minutes too late**. So a 15:00 start would not comply.\n\n**The latest you could start is 14:30 UTC**, which would get you to 100% traffic by 16:00 UTC (assuming each stage runs its full minimum duration with no pauses)."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-006", "category": "your_data", "title": "Incident chat log retention", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1030, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 18, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4063, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4060}, "answer_chars": 81, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 55, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4269, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4266}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer matches section 10.1 and the reference: incident channel chat logs are retained for 400 days and then deleted automatically.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja34d975a-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja03577a8-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:20-0500", "answer": "Incident channel chat logs are kept for **400 days**, then deleted automatically."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-003", "category": "your_data", "title": "Platinum downtime budget", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4295, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 281, "reasoning_tokens": 146, "input_tokens": 4085, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4082}, "answer_chars": 493, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 70, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4490, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly calculates the Platinum downtime thresholds and credit amounts, and its additional request-deadline and contract-precedence details are supported by the handbook.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja16a3659-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja0355093-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:21-0500", "answer": "For a 30-day month, the Platinum **99.95% API uptime commitment** allows **21.6 minutes of downtime (21 minutes, 36 seconds)** before a service credit applies.\n\n- **More than 21.6 minutes:** credit of **10% of that month\u2019s fees**.\n- **More than 432 minutes (7 hours, 12 minutes)**\u2014uptime below 99.0%: credit of **25% of that month\u2019s fees**.\n\nCustomers must request credits within **30 days after the affected month ends**. A signed customer contract overrides the handbook if its terms differ."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-006", "category": "your_data", "title": "Incident chat log retention", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 778, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 28, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4288, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4224}, "answer_chars": 130, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 45, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4278, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer accurately states the documented retention period of 400 days followed by automatic deletion.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja34d9759-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja03577a8-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:21-0500", "answer": "The document states that **incident channel chat logs** are retained for **400 days**, after which they are deleted automatically."}
