{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-008", "category": "your_data", "title": "Friday deploy with the standard canary", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4367, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 230, "reasoning_tokens": 118, "input_tokens": 4083, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4080}, "answer_chars": 331, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 131, "reasoning_tokens": 30, "input_tokens": 4500, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 4, "reason": "The answer correctly rejects 15:00 and calculates the 90-minute rollout, but gives a start before 14:30 rather than the rubric's required latest start of 14:30, while faithfully interpreting the document's strict 'before 16:00' wording.", "correct": false, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja110514d-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja03577a9-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:22-0500", "answer": "No. Friday deploys must reach **100% of traffic before 16:00 UTC**. A Normal rollout requires:\n- **5%** for 30 minutes.\n- **25%** for 60 minutes.\n- Then **100%**.\n\nStarting at 15:00 would reach 100% at 16:30\u2014too late. You must start **before 14:30 UTC** to meet the strict \u201cbefore 16:00\u201d cutoff, allowing extra time for any delays."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-003", "category": "your_data", "title": "Platinum downtime budget", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 7707, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 782, "reasoning_tokens": 621, "input_tokens": 4143, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4076}, "answer_chars": 556, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2028, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 57, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4518, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly calculates 21.6 minutes of allowed downtime and states the documented 10% and 25% credit thresholds and request deadline.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja16a365b-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja0355093-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:23-0500", "answer": "For a Platinum customer in a 30-day month:\n\n**Allowed downtime:** 21.6 minutes (21 minutes 36 seconds) of API downtime before you breach the 99.95% monthly uptime commitment.\n- Calculation: 30 days \u00d7 24 hours \u00d7 60 minutes = 43,200 minutes total; 0.05% of 43,200 = 21.6 minutes\n\n**Service credit if you miss the commitment:**\n- If monthly uptime falls below 99.95%: **10% of that month's fees**\n- If monthly uptime falls below 99.0%: **25% of that month's fees**\n\nCustomers must request credits within 30 days of the end of the affected month (section 8.3)."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-002", "category": "your_data", "title": "Escalating an unmitigated API error spike", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2913, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 181, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4092, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4089}, "answer_chars": 745, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 137, "reasoning_tokens": 46, "input_tokens": 4642, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 4, "reason": "The answer correctly states SEV-2 and all escalation thresholds, but unlike the reference and rubric it does not say the service owner should already have been paged, instead offering a document-supported conditional calculation based on declaration time.", "correct": false, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja37334e0-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja0355095-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:24-0500", "answer": "This meets **SEV-2** criteria: API errors above 5% for 10 consecutive minutes.\n\nEscalation timers run from **declaration**, not when errors started:\n- **At declaration:** page the on-call primary. Beacon pages the secondary if the primary hasn\u2019t acknowledged within **15 minutes**.\n- **After 45 minutes without mitigation:** page the owning team\u2019s service owner (Tier 2).\n\nIf you declared when the 10-minute threshold was reached, you\u2019re about 40 minutes into the incident; the service-owner escalation is due in about 5 minutes.\n\nPage the **Director of Reliability (Tier 3)** if either:\n- This SEV-2 lasts **more than 3 hours from declaration to resolution**, even if mitigated; or\n- It is the **third SEV-2 on the same service within 7 days**."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-006", "category": "your_data", "title": "Incident chat log retention", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5834, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 27, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4119, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 124, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 56, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4280, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4277}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer accurately states the section 10.1 retention policy: incident channel chat logs are kept for 400 days and then deleted automatically.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja34d9756-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja03577a8-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:24-0500", "answer": "According to section 10.1 of the handbook, incident channel chat logs are kept for **400 days**, then deleted automatically."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-005", "category": "your_data", "title": "Time in lieu for overnight incidents", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4544, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 461, "reasoning_tokens": 331, "input_tokens": 4151, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4076}, "answer_chars": 472, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1305, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 64, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4471, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly awards 8 hours for the two incidents lasting more than 45 minutes and states that the time must be used within 30 days of each incident or it expires.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja40318f7-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja0355096-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:25-0500", "answer": "You're owed **8 hours** of time in lieu.\n\nPer section 5, you get 4 hours of time off for each **overnight** incident lasting **more than 45 minutes**:\n\n- 30 minutes \u2014 doesn't qualify (not more than 45 minutes)\n- 70 minutes \u2014 qualifies \u2192 4 hours\n- 2 hours \u2014 qualifies \u2192 4 hours\n\n**Total: 8 hours.**\n\nYou must take the time in lieu **within 30 days of each incident**, or it expires. Since these were last week, your deadlines fall roughly 30 days from each incident's date."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-002", "category": "your_data", "title": "Escalating an unmitigated API error spike", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6039, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 390, "reasoning_tokens": 194, "input_tokens": 4092, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4089}, "answer_chars": 794, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 72, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4651, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies SEV-2, the primary and conditional secondary paging, Tier 2 escalation after 45 minutes without mitigation, and both Tier 3 triggers, while accurately clarifying that timing starts at declaration.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja37334e1-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja0355095-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:25-0500", "answer": "This meets the **SEV-2** criterion: API errors above 5% for 10 consecutive minutes.\n\nWho should be paged:\n- **On-call primary:** at declaration.\n- **Secondary:** automatically if the primary doesn\u2019t acknowledge within 15 minutes.\n- **Owning team\u2019s service owner (Tier 2):** if there\u2019s still no mitigation 45 minutes after declaration.\n\n**Timing matters:** escalation clocks start at declaration, not when errors began. If you declared 50 minutes ago, the service owner should already have been paged. If the errors started 50 minutes ago, check the declaration timestamp.\n\nPage the **Director of Reliability (Tier 3)** when either:\n- The SEV-2 remains **unresolved for more than 3 hours after declaration**, even if mitigated; or\n- This is the **third SEV-2 on the same service within 7 days**."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-002", "category": "your_data", "title": "Escalating an unmitigated API error spike", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4696, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 344, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4149, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4076}, "answer_chars": 1340, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 203, "reasoning_tokens": 37, "input_tokens": 4798, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 4, "reason": "The answer satisfies the core rubric with the correct SEV-2 classification, Tier 2 escalation and both Tier 3 triggers, but adds an unsupported timing assumption and slightly misstates the optional SEV-1 thresholds.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": ["Saying Tier 2 paging should have happened approximately 5 minutes ago assumes declaration occurred when the elevated error rate began; the document measures escalation from declaration.", "The optional SEV-1 escalation summary says 'at 60 minutes' and 'at 2 hours,' whereas the document requires lasting more than 60 minutes and more than 2 hours."], "faithful": false}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja37334de-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja0355095-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:27-0500", "answer": "Based on the handbook, here's the situation:\n\n**What severity this is:** An API error rate above 5% for 10 consecutive minutes is a **SEV-2 (Major)** \u2014 and it's been ~50 minutes, so it's well past that threshold.\n\n**Who should have been paged by now:**\n\n| Tier | Who | When |\n|---|---|---|\n| Tier 1 | On-call primary (secondary as backup) | At declaration |\n| Tier 2 | The owning team's service owner | A SEV-2 with no mitigation after **45 minutes** \u2014 so this should have happened ~5 minutes ago |\n| Tier 3 | Director of Reliability | A SEV-2 lasting more than **3 hours**, or the third SEV-2 on the same service within 7 days |\n\nAlso note: Beacon auto-escalates if a page isn't acknowledged \u2014 after 15 minutes for a SEV-2 \u2014 so the secondary should already have been paged if the primary didn't acknowledge.\n\n**What would escalate this to the Director of Reliability (Tier 3):**\n- The SEV-2 lasts more than **3 hours** (measured from declaration to resolution, not mitigation), **or**\n- It's the **third SEV-2 on the same service within 7 days**\n\nIf it instead became a SEV-1 (e.g., full API outage in a region, suspected data exposure, or >25% of active customers impacted), the Director of Reliability would be paged at **60 minutes**, and the VP of Engineering and CTO at **2 hours** or immediately for suspected customer data exposure."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-004", "category": "your_data", "title": "Security patch during the holiday freeze", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 16018, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1689, "reasoning_tokens": 1415, "input_tokens": 4139, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 1052, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 5648, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 68, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4646, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies the holiday freeze exception for CVSS 9.0+ patches, requires VP of Engineering approval and progressive rollout, includes timely CAB logging, and accurately adds applicable Normal-change requirements.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja07aa0e1-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja03577a7-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:30-0500", "answer": "**Yes.** December 22 falls inside the holiday freeze (December 18 \u2013 January 4, per section 7.4), during which only Standard and Emergency changes are normally allowed. However, there's an explicit exception: a patch for a security vulnerability rated **CVSS 9.0 or higher** may ship as a **Normal change** with approval from the **VP of Engineering**. A CVSS 9.3 patch qualifies.\n\nWhat you need:\n\n- **Approval from the VP of Engineering** (required by the freeze exception).\n- As a Normal change, it also needs **one approval from the owning team** (Warehouse Sync). If the patch is a schema migration, network/ACL change, or authentication change, it additionally needs **CAB approval** (section 7.1).\n- It must still follow the **progressive rollout** in section 7.3 (canary at 5% for 30 min \u2192 25% for 60 min \u2192 100%), and the normal **deploy windows** in section 7.2 still apply (Mon\u2013Thu 14:00\u201320:00 UTC; Friday changes must reach 100% of traffic before 16:00 UTC).\n- The **freeze exception must be logged in the CAB register within 1 business day**."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-002", "category": "your_data", "title": "Escalating an unmitigated API error spike", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 17118, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 2016, "reasoning_tokens": 1800, "input_tokens": 4149, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4076}, "answer_chars": 820, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 7210, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 65, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4679, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies SEV-2, the primary and Tier 2 paging requirements, and both SEV-2 Director escalation triggers, with additional escalation details supported by the handbook.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja37334df-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja0355095-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:37-0500", "answer": "This is a **SEV-2**: API error rate above 5% for 10 consecutive minutes.\n\nBy ~50 minutes with no mitigation, these should have been paged:\n\n- **Tier 1:** on-call primary at declaration; **secondary** automatically if the primary didn\u2019t acknowledge within the SEV-2 target of **15 minutes**.\n- **Tier 2:** the owning team\u2019s **service owner**, because a SEV-2 has had **no mitigation after 45 minutes** \u2014 so by ~50 minutes.\n\nIt goes up to the **Director of Reliability (Tier 3)** if:\n\n- this **SEV-2 lasts more than 3 hours** \u2014 measured from declaration to **resolution**, not mitigation;\n- it is the **third SEV-2 on the same service within 7 days**; or\n- it is raised to **SEV-1** and lasts **more than 60 minutes**.\n\nSeparately, suspected customer data exposure pages **VP of Engineering and CTO immediately** (Tier 4)."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-008", "category": "your_data", "title": "Friday deploy with the standard canary", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 24804, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 3130, "reasoning_tokens": 2938, "input_tokens": 4141, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4076}, "answer_chars": 585, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 9928, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 161, "reasoning_tokens": 39, "input_tokens": 4586, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 3, "reason": "The answer correctly rejects 15:00 and calculates the 90-minute rollout, but its final latest-start recommendation of 14:29 UTC differs from the rubric\u2019s required 14:30 UTC and assumes unsupported minute-level granularity.", "correct": false, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": ["The claim that 14:29 UTC is the strictly safe latest start introduces a whole-minute restriction not specified in the handbook."], "faithful": false}}, "workflow_id": "0sfja110514c-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfja03577a9-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:43-0500", "answer": "No \u2014 15:00 UTC on Friday is too late.\n\nPer \u00a77.2, on **Friday** a production deploy may start from **14:00 UTC**, but the change **must reach 100% of traffic before 16:00 UTC**. A Normal change\u2019s progressive rollout (\u00a77.3) takes **90 minutes** to get to 100%: 30 min canary at 5% + 60 min at 25%.\n\n- 15:00 start \u2192 100% at **16:30** \u2192 misses the cutoff.\n- Working back from \u201c100% before 16:00\u201d: latest start is **14:30 UTC** (lands exactly at 16:00). Because the rule says *before* 16:00, the strictly safe latest is **14:29 UTC** \u2014 i.e., start between **14:00 and 14:29 UTC** on Friday."}
