{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-011", "category": "your_data", "title": "On-call exemption after parental leave", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3509, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 356, "reasoning_tokens": 293, "input_tokens": 4124, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 325, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1276, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 62, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4339, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"pass": true, "said_not_in_doc": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly states that the handbook does not address parental-leave exemptions and accurately distinguishes the 60-day new-hire eligibility rule from any return-from-leave policy.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfjb450ee01-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjb3b6e8bc-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:51-0500", "answer": "The document doesn't cover an on-call exemption for engineers returning from parental leave. The handbook only mentions eligibility timing for **new hires** (joining the rotation no earlier than 60 days after their start date), but says nothing about parental leave or any exemption period for engineers returning from leave."}
{"run_id": "full-r2", "item_id": "your_data-009", "category": "your_data", "title": "Weekly on-call pay with extra pages", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6442, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 817, "reasoning_tokens": 644, "input_tokens": 4133, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 645, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2686, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 59, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4466, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly calculates $810 from the $450 primary stipend plus three additional pages at $120 each, and its additional notes are supported by the handbook.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfjb3de07d1-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjb3b6e8bd-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:29:53-0500", "answer": "Based on Section 5 (On-call compensation) of the handbook:\n\n**Your pay for that week: $810**\n\n- **Weekly stipend (primary):** $450\n- **Page pay:** The stipend covers the first 5 out-of-hours pages. You had 8 out-of-hours pages, so 3 additional pages \u00d7 $120 = **$360**\n\n**Total: $450 + $360 = $810**\n\nOne caveat: if any of those pages were **overnight incidents** (22:00\u201306:00 local time) lasting more than 45 minutes, you'd also earn 4 hours of time in lieu per such incident, which must be taken within 30 days or it expires.\n\nAlso note: compensation is submitted through the payroll on-call form by the 3rd business day of the following month."}
